"use strict";
module.exports = /*#__PURE__*/JSON.parse('[{"chapter":1,"verse":1,"order":1,"speaker":"Dhritarashtra","essence":"The war begins in a question, not a sword strike.","snippet":"Dhritarashtra said: O Sanjaya, what did my sons and the sons of Pandu do, assembled on the holy field of Kurukshetra and eager for battle?","tags":["kurukshetra","dhritarashtra","sanjaya","opening-scene","battlefield"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":2,"order":2,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"War becomes real the moment the enemy is seen clearly.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Seeing the Pandava army arranged in battle formation, King Duryodhana went to Dronacharya and spoke these words.","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","dronacharya","pandava-army","battle-formation"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":3,"order":3,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"A battlefield can be won first by how it is described.","snippet":"O teacher, look at this great army of the sons of Pandu, arranged in battle formation by your wise disciple, the son of Drupada.","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","drona","pandava-army","battle-prelude"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":4,"order":4,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"The other side is strong, and pretending otherwise changes nothing.","snippet":"Here in the Pandava army are mighty warriors, great archers, equal to Bhima and Arjuna in battle: Satyaki, Virata, and the great chariot-…","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","pandava-army","battlefield","maharatha"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":5,"order":5,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The battlefield is already full of power and named allies.","snippet":"Dhृष्टकेतु, Chekitana, and the valiant king of Kashi; Purujit, Kuntibhoja, and Shaibya, the best among men.","tags":["kurukshetra","pandava-army","warriors","sanjaya","battlefield"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":6,"order":6,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"The enemy line is full of elite fighters.","snippet":"Yudhamanyu, brave and powerful, Uttamaujas, brave and powerful, Subhadra\'s son, and the sons of Draupadi — all of them are great warriors.","tags":["kurukshetra","pandava-army","maharatha","duryodhana","battlefield-list"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":7,"order":7,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"Pride counts its own strength when fear is near.","snippet":"O best of the twice-born, note also our own chief warriors. I name them to remind you of our army.","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","army-listing","battlefield","drona"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":8,"order":8,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"Fear clings to strength by naming it aloud.","snippet":"Bhishma, Karna, Kripa, Ashvatthama, Vikarna, and the son of Somadatta are also there.","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","bhishma","karna","army-list"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":9,"order":9,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"Confidence built on numbers still trembles before battle.","snippet":"Besides these, many heroes have given up their lives for my sake. They wield many kinds of weapons and are all skilled in warfare.","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","battlefield","kuru-army","warriors"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":10,"order":10,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"Fear can declare defeat before the battle starts.","snippet":"Our force, guarded by Bhishma, is insufficient; their force, guarded by Bhima, is sufficient.","tags":["kurukshetra","duryodhana","bhishma","bhima","battlefield"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":11,"order":11,"speaker":"Duryodhana","essence":"Victory begins with disciplined formation, not scattered strength.","snippet":"Remain at your stations on every front and protect Bhishma from all sides.","tags":["kurukshetra","bhishma","duryodhana","battle-formation","army-command"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":12,"order":12,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"A single battle cry can turn fear into momentum.","snippet":"The elder of the Kuru clan, the powerful grandfather Bhishma, roared like a lion and blew his conch loudly, filling Duryodhana with joy.","tags":["kurukshetra","bhishma","duryodhana","conch-blast","kaurava-army"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":13,"order":13,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The war announces itself before the first blow.","snippet":"Then conches, kettledrums, drums, and trumpets burst forth at once. Their sound became thunderous.","tags":["kurukshetra","conch-blowing","battlefield-noise","bhishma","kaurava-army"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":14,"order":14,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Resolve answers chaos before words begin.","snippet":"Then, seated on the great chariot yoked with white horses, Madhava and Pandava blew their divine conches.","tags":["kurukshetra","shankha","chariot","krishna-arjuna","battlefield"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":15,"order":15,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The war begins in sound before a single strike.","snippet":"Hrisikesha Krishna blew the Panchajanya, Dhananjaya Arjuna blew the Devadatta, and Bhima of mighty deeds blew the great conch Paundra.","tags":["kurukshetra","conch-blowing","panchajanya","devadatta","paundra"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":16,"order":16,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The war begins to answer back in sound.","snippet":"King Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, blew the Anantavijaya; Nakula and Sahadeva blew the Sughosha and Manipushpaka.","tags":["conch-blowing","kurukshetra","pandava-brothers","battlefield","yudhishthira"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":17,"order":17,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Names and conches turn hesitation into commitment.","snippet":"The great archer from Kashi, Shikhandi the great warrior, Dhrishtadyumna, Virata, and invincible Satyaki.","tags":["kurukshetra","conch-blowing","pandava-allies","battlefield-roll-call","sanjaya"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":18,"order":18,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Allied resolve announces itself before the battle starts.","snippet":"Drupada, Draupadi\'s sons, and mighty Abhimanyu each blew their conches separately, O lord of the earth.","tags":["kurukshetra","conch-blowing","pandava-army","abhimanyu","drupada"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":19,"order":19,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"A single sound can break resolve before battle begins.","snippet":"That terrible sound split the hearts of Dhritarashtra\'s side, echoing through sky and earth.","tags":["kurukshetra","sankha-nada","duryodhana","pandava-army","battlefield-omen"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":20,"order":20,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The battle reaches its threshold, and action begins before words do.","snippet":"Then, seeing the sons of Dhritarashtra standing in battle order while the weapons were about to begin, Arjuna lifted his bow.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","gandiva","battlefield","dhritarashtra"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":21,"order":21,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clear sight comes before decisive action.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Hrishikesha, place my chariot between the two armies, O Achyuta, until I can look at these men who wish to fight and see w…","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","chariot","battlefield","pause"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":22,"order":22,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clear seeing comes before irreversible action.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Achyuta, keep my chariot between the two armies until I can inspect these men standing here, eager for battle, and see wit…","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","battlefield","hesitation","clear-seeing"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":23,"order":23,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Conflict becomes real when you look at the people involved.","snippet":"I want to see those who have gathered here, eager to fight and wishing to please the evil-minded son of Dhritarashtra.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","duryodhana","battlefield","prewar"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":24,"order":24,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The chariot is placed where choice becomes unavoidable.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Spoken to thus by Gudakesha, Hrishikesha stationed the finest chariot between the two armies, in front of Bhishma, Drona, a…","tags":["kurukshetra","sanjaya","arjuna","rathottama","battlefield"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":25,"order":25,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing the people involved makes denial impossible.","snippet":"Standing before Bhishma, Drona, and all the rulers, Krishna said, \\"O Partha, behold these assembled Kurus.\\"","tags":["kurukshetra","bhishma","drona","chariot","scene-setting"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":26,"order":26,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Recognition turns battle into sorrow.","snippet":"Then Arjuna, son of Pritha, saw fathers, grandfathers, teachers, maternal uncles, brothers, sons, grandsons, friends, fathers-in-law, and…","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","family-relation","battlefield-vision","bhishma-drona"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":27,"order":27,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The battle becomes unbearable when every side is family.","snippet":"Seeing all his relatives standing there, Arjuna sank into grief and spoke in fear.","tags":["kurukshetra","family-conflict","arjuna-grief","relatives","battlefield-dharma"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":28,"order":28,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Compassion can stop the warrior before the first arrow flies.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Seeing my own people gathered here, eager for battle, I am overcome with pity and grief, O Krishna.","tags":["arjuna-vishada","karuna","kurukshetra","relatives","battlefield-grief"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":29,"order":29,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The body reveals fear before the mind can explain it.","snippet":"My limbs are failing, my mouth is drying up, my body trembles, and my hair stands on end.","tags":["arjuna-vishada","kurukshetra","bodily-fear","overwhelm","trembling"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":30,"order":30,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Fear strips away control before a single arrow is released.","snippet":"My bow slips from my hand. My skin burns. I cannot stand steady, and my mind reels.","tags":["arjuna","kurukshetra","gandiva","panic","physical-collapse"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":31,"order":31,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"A victory that destroys your own people is not worth having.","snippet":"O Keshava, I see only inauspicious signs, and I see no good in killing my own people in battle.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna-vishada","inauspicious-signs","family-conflict","moral-doubt"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":32,"order":32,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Victory means nothing when the price is the destruction of what you love.","snippet":"I do not desire victory, Krishna, nor kingdom, nor pleasures. What use is kingdom to us, Govinda? What use are pleasures or even life?","tags":["arjuna-vishada","battlefield-crisis","vairagya","despair","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":33,"order":33,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The prize is empty when the people attached to it stand in the line of fire.","snippet":"Those for whom we wanted kingdom, pleasures, and comfort stand here in battle, ready to give up life and wealth.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna-vishada","family-conflict","battlefield","relatives"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":34,"order":34,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Blood ties make victory feel like loss.","snippet":"Teachers, fathers, sons, grandfathers, maternal uncles, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other relatives.","tags":["kurukshetra","family-relations","arjuna-grief","kinship","battlefield-conflict"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":35,"order":35,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"No prize can justify killing what is sacred to you.","snippet":"I do not want to kill these people, even if they kill me, O Madhusudana. Not even for the rule of the three worlds, much less for the earth.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna-vishada","kinship","nonviolence","moral-conflict"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":36,"order":36,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Violence against kin brings no joy; it only deepens the wound.","snippet":"O Janardana, what joy would come to us by killing these sons of Dhritarashtra? Killing these aggressors would only bring us sin.","tags":["kinship","moral-anguish","kurukshetra","ahimsa","family-war"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":37,"order":37,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Kinship makes violence feel unbearable.","snippet":"Therefore, we are not fit to kill our own kinsmen, the sons of Dhritarashtra. How could we be happy after killing our relatives, O Madhava?","tags":["arjuna-vishada","kinship","nonviolence","kurukshetra","family-conflict"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":38,"order":38,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Greed blinds people to the damage they are causing.","snippet":"Though greed has blinded them, they do not see the fault in destroying a family or the wrong in betraying friends.","tags":["lobha","kula-ksaya","mitra-droha","arjuna-vishada","family-conflict"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":39,"order":39,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clear sight makes withdrawal from harm the only sane choice.","snippet":"Why should we not turn away from this sin, when we clearly see the fault in destroying the family, O Janardana?","tags":["kulaksaya","family-destruction","moral-refusal","arjuna-doubt","adharma"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":40,"order":40,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Destroy the family, and the moral order inside it collapses.","snippet":"When a family falls apart, its ancient duties disappear. When duty is lost, wrongdoing overtakes the whole family.","tags":["kuladharma","family-destruction","adharma","lineage","arjuna-grief"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":41,"order":41,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"When order breaks, the damage spreads into future generations.","snippet":"When lawlessness grows, the women of the family are corrupted. When women are corrupted, mixed social disorder is born.","tags":["kuladharma","adharma","varnasankara","family-order","arjuna-grief"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":42,"order":42,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Breaking family order is imagined as ruin that reaches even the dead.","snippet":"Mixed lineage leads the destroyers of family to ruin, and their ancestors fall because offerings of food and water stop.","tags":["kuladharma","varnasankara","pindodaka","pitrs","arjuna-vishada"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":43,"order":43,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"When conduct breaks, the inherited order that protects everyone breaks too.","snippet":"Because of these faults that create mixed social order, the eternal duties of family and community are destroyed.","tags":["kuladharma","jativarna","family-order","social-disruption","arjuna-grief"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":44,"order":44,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Breaking family duty brings suffering that lasts beyond one lifetime.","snippet":"O Janardana, we have always heard that those whose family duties are destroyed dwell long in a lower realm.","tags":["kuladharma","family-duty","arjuna-vishada","kurukshetra","adharma"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":45,"order":45,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Greed can make even victory feel like a crime.","snippet":"Alas, we have resolved to commit a grave wrong—driven by greed for kingdom and pleasure, we are ready to kill our own kin.","tags":["kinship","moral-crisis","greed","arjuna-vishada","violence"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":46,"order":46,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Harming loved ones feels worse than losing your own life.","snippet":"If the armed sons of Dhritarashtra were to kill me in battle while I stood unresisting and without weapons, that would be far better for me.","tags":["arjuna-vishada","kurukshetra","kinship-conflict","moral-dilemma","nonviolence"]},{"chapter":1,"verse":47,"order":47,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Grief can make even a warrior lay down his weapons.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Saying this, Arjuna sat down on the chariot seat in the midst of the battlefield, casting aside his bow and arrows, his min…","tags":["arjuna","kurukshetra","despair","chariot","battlefield"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":1,"order":48,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Grief opens the door for instruction.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: To Arjuna, overcome by pity, his eyes full of tears and clouded with grief, Madhusudana spoke these words.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","sanjaya","grief","krishna"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":2,"order":49,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Delusion has no place in a decisive moment.","snippet":"Krishna said: Arjuna, where has this delusion come from in this crisis? Noble people do not follow it. It does not lead upward, and it br…","tags":["arjuna","krishna-rebuke","kurukshetra","kshatra-dharma","cowardice"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":3,"order":50,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Weakness is optional; the call to act remains.","snippet":"Do not yield to weakness, Partha. It does not suit you. Cast off this petty weakness of heart and rise, scorcher of foes.","tags":["arjuna","kurukshetra","hredaudurbalya","partha","courage"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":4,"order":51,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Respect can make necessary action feel unbearable.","snippet":"Arjuna said: How can I fight Bhishma and Drona with arrows in battle, O Madhusudana? They are worthy of worship, O destroyer of enemies.","tags":["arjuna","bhishma","drona","kurukshetra","moral-conflict"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":5,"order":52,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"A victory that destroys reverence is already a loss.","snippet":"It is better to live on alms in this world than to kill these great teachers. If I kill them, the pleasures I enjoy here will be stained …","tags":["guru","arjuna-dilemma","kurukshetra","moral-cost","bhiksha"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":6,"order":53,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Honest uncertainty is the first crack in moral paralysis.","snippet":"We do not know which is better for us: to fight or not to fight. We do not even know whether we will conquer them or they us. The sons of…","tags":["arjuna-doubt","kurukshetra","moral-conflict","dhritarashtra-lineage","battlefield-paralysis"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":7,"order":54,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clarity begins when you admit you cannot see the right action alone.","snippet":"My nature is overwhelmed by weakness, and my mind is confused about duty. I ask you: tell me with certainty what is best for me. I am you…","tags":["arjuna-vishada","dharma-sankat","sharanagati","guru-upadesha","inquiry"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":8,"order":55,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"No outer victory can cure an inner collapse.","snippet":"Even if I gained an unrivaled, prosperous kingdom on earth or lordship over the gods, I see nothing that could remove this grief that dri…","tags":["arjuna-vishada","grief","kurukshetra","inner-collapse","attachment"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":9,"order":56,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Refusal has stopped the war inside him.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Having spoken thus to Hrishikesha, Gudakesha, the scorcher of foes, said to Govinda, “I will not fight,” and fell silent.","tags":["arjuna","sanjaya","kurukshetra","refusal","silence"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":10,"order":57,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Guidance begins when grief is met without rejection.","snippet":"Hṛṣīkeśa spoke to the grieving Arjuna, smiling slightly, in the midst of the two armies.","tags":["kurukshetra","arjuna","hृषीकेśa","battlefield","grief"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":11,"order":58,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing ends grief where the wise know none is needed.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: You grieve for what should not be grieved for, yet speak words of wisdom. The wise do not grieve for the dead or t…","tags":["shoka","pandita","viveka","grief","death"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":12,"order":59,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What truly exists was never born and never lost.","snippet":"I was never absent, nor were you, nor these kings. Nor will any of us cease to be in the future.","tags":["atman","death","immortality","kurukshetra","body"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":13,"order":60,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What changes form is not what you truly are.","snippet":"Just as the embodied one passes through childhood, youth, and old age in this body, so too it passes into another body. The wise are not …","tags":["dehantara","atman","birth-and-death","impermanence","sankhya"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":14,"order":61,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Passing sensations lose power when you stop treating them as permanent.","snippet":"Contacts with the senses, O son of Kunti, bring heat and cold, pleasure and pain. They come and go; they are impermanent. Endure them, O …","tags":["titiksha","sense-contacts","impermanence","equanimity","krishna-to-arjuna"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":15,"order":62,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins where pain and pleasure stop controlling you.","snippet":"The wise person who is not shaken by these, and remains equal in pain and pleasure, becomes fit for freedom.","tags":["samaduhkhasukha","dhira","amritatva","equanimity","sense-contact"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":16,"order":63,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What passes away was never ultimate; what is real cannot vanish.","snippet":"The unreal has no being; the real has no nonbeing. Seers have understood the boundary of both.","tags":["sat-asat","tattvadarshi","impermanence","reality","duality"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":17,"order":64,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What truly pervades everything cannot be destroyed.","snippet":"Know that to be imperishable by which this entire world is pervaded. No one can destroy this imperishable reality.","tags":["imperishable","nitya","atman","pervasion","deathlessness"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":18,"order":65,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is truly you cannot be destroyed, so duty remains.","snippet":"These bodies are said to be finite, but the embodied being is eternal, indestructible, and immeasurable. Therefore, fight, Arjuna.","tags":["dehin","nitya","anashina","body-mortality","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":19,"order":66,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you are cannot be reduced to killer or victim.","snippet":"Whoever thinks this imperishable being is the killer, and whoever thinks it is killed, both do not understand. It neither kills nor is ki…","tags":["atma","deathlessness","nonduality","identification","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":20,"order":67,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you are cannot be touched by birth or death.","snippet":"It is never born and never dies. It did not come into being, and it will not cease. Unborn, eternal, everlasting, ancient, it is not dest…","tags":["atman","birth-and-death","imperishability","body","krishna-teaching"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":21,"order":68,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing makes violence look absurd.","snippet":"One who knows the imperishable, eternal, unborn, and unchanging cannot think of killing or causing death.","tags":["atman","death","nonviolence","immortality","clarity"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":22,"order":69,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you are does not end when one body is left behind.","snippet":"As a person discards worn-out clothes and puts on new ones, the embodied being discards worn-out bodies and enters new ones.","tags":["dehi","body-as-clothing","transmigration","atma","impermanence"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":23,"order":70,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your deepest reality is beyond every physical force.","snippet":"Weapons cannot cut it, fire cannot burn it, water cannot wet it, and wind cannot dry it.","tags":["atman","indestructible self","kurukshetra","physical elements","immortality"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":24,"order":71,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you are cannot be harmed by anything that changes.","snippet":"This embodied self cannot be cut, burned, wetted, or dried. It is eternal, all-pervading, unmoving, fixed, and timeless.","tags":["atman","imperishability","nitya","sarvagata","dehī"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":25,"order":72,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is deepest in you was never available for loss.","snippet":"It is unseen, beyond thought, and said to be unchanged. Therefore, knowing it this way, you should not grieve.","tags":["atman","avyakta","avikarya","grief","immortality"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":26,"order":73,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even the plain fact of change is no reason to drown in sorrow.","snippet":"O mighty-armed one, even if you think this embodied being is always born and always dies, you still should not grieve like this.","tags":["janma-mrityu","shoka","embodied-being","kurukshetra","grief"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":27,"order":74,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What must change is not a reason for grief.","snippet":"For what is born, death is certain; for what dies, birth is certain. What cannot be avoided should not be grieved over.","tags":["birth-death-cycle","impermanence","mortal-body","grief","sankhya"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":28,"order":75,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What appears briefly was never meant to be clung to.","snippet":"All beings are unmanifest before birth and unmanifest after death; they are manifest only in between. Why grieve over that?","tags":["birth-and-death","impermanence","lamentation","kurukshetra","atman-body"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":29,"order":76,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The true self remains mysterious even after endless hearing.","snippet":"Some behold the inner being as wondrous; some speak of it as wondrous; some hear of it as wondrous; and even after hearing, no one truly …","tags":["atman","durvijneya","self-knowledge","wonder","direct-realisation"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":30,"order":77,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is most real in a person cannot be killed, so grief loses its ground.","snippet":"O descendant of Bharata, the embodied one in every body is eternal and cannot be slain. Therefore you should not grieve for any being.","tags":["dehi","immortality","body","grief","atman"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":31,"order":78,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action can feel hard and still be the best choice.","snippet":"Considering your own duty, you should not waver. For a warrior, no action is more beneficial than a righteous battle.","tags":["swadharma","kshatriya-dharma","righteous-battle","wavering","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":32,"order":79,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A righteous burden can become the highest opening.","snippet":"An unbidden battle is an open gate to higher realms. O Partha, fortunate are the warriors who receive such a war.","tags":["kshatriya-dharma","righteous-battle","svargadvara","kurukshetra","duty-under-pressure"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":33,"order":80,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Avoiding the right duty does not protect you; it stains you.","snippet":"If you do not fight this righteous war, you will abandon your duty and honor and incur blame.","tags":["svadharma","kshatriya-dharma","honor","blame","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":34,"order":81,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A honored life can be wounded more by shame than by death.","snippet":"And all beings will speak of your everlasting disgrace. For an honored person, disgrace is worse than death.","tags":["akirti","honor","shame","kshatriya","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":35,"order":82,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Retreat from duty, and respect turns to shrinkage.","snippet":"The great warriors will think you withdrew from battle out of fear. Those who once held you in high regard will see you as small.","tags":["arjuna","kurukshetra","kshatriya-honor","fear-of-retreat","swadharma"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":36,"order":83,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Public shame can hurt more than physical danger.","snippet":"Your enemies will speak many unworthy words, mocking your strength. What could be more painful than that?","tags":["public-shame","cowardice","arjuna-doubt","battlefield-pressure","honour"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":37,"order":84,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Act now; the result does not cancel the duty.","snippet":"If you are killed, you will attain heaven; if you win, you will enjoy the kingdom. Therefore, rise, Kaunteya, and fight with resolve.","tags":["kurukshetra","resolve","battle-duty","outcome","kshatriya"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":38,"order":85,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equanimity frees action from the stain of panic and craving.","snippet":"Treat pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat alike. Then enter the battle; you will not incur wrongdoing.","tags":["samatva","jayajaya","labhalabhau","karmayoga","battlefield"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":39,"order":86,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear understanding frees action from bondage.","snippet":"This wisdom has been taught to you in Sankhya. Now hear it in yoga. Equipped with this understanding, Arjuna, you will cast off the bonda…","tags":["sankhya","buddhi","karmabandha","karma-yoga","jñana"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":40,"order":87,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even a tiny start on the right path protects you from fear.","snippet":"In this human world, no effort toward this steady wisdom is ever lost. No harmful result comes from it. Even a little practice of this dh…","tags":["karma-yoga","steady-wisdom","small-practice","fearlessness","dharma"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":41,"order":88,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Resolute seeing unifies the mind; hesitation multiplies it.","snippet":"O son of the Kurus, the resolute intellect is one-pointed here. The intellect of the irresolute is many-branched and endless.","tags":["resolute-intellect","one-pointed-mind","indecision","vyavasaya","mental-fragmentation"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":42,"order":89,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Beautiful words can hide a mind trapped by desire.","snippet":"The unwise speak flowery words. They delight in the ritual sections of the Vedas and say nothing else exists.","tags":["vedavada","kama","ritualism","delusion","flowery-speech"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":43,"order":90,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Flowery promises can keep desire alive while pretending to guide you.","snippet":"Those without clear seeing speak flowery words that promise birth and action-fruit, and describe many rites for enjoyment and power.","tags":["kamatmānaḥ","svargapara","flowery speech","ritualism","desire-driven action"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":44,"order":91,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Craving scatters the mind before wisdom can settle.","snippet":"For those whose minds are carried away by pleasure and power, steadfast determination in meditation does not arise.","tags":["bhog","aishvarya","vyavasayika-buddhi","samadhi","attachment"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":45,"order":92,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when gain and loss stop defining you.","snippet":"The Vedas deal with the three qualities. Arjuna, rise beyond the three qualities, beyond opposites, fixed in lasting reality, free from c…","tags":["triguna","nirdvandva","yogakshema","nityasattva","vairagya"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":46,"order":93,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Complete understanding makes lesser sources unnecessary.","snippet":"For one who understands, all the Vedas are as useful as a small puddle when a great reservoir of water is at hand.","tags":["vedas","brahmajna","knowledge","reservoir","scriptural-limits"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":47,"order":94,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action belongs to you; the result does not.","snippet":"You have a right to action alone, never to its fruits. Do not become the cause of the result, and do not cling to inaction.","tags":["karma-yoga","nishkama","attachment","outcome","duty"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":48,"order":95,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equanimity turns action into yoga.","snippet":"O Dhananjaya, perform actions while established in yoga, abandoning attachment. Remain equal in success and failure, for equanimity is ca…","tags":["equanimity","samatva","karma-yoga","attachment","success-failure"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":49,"order":96,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear discernment is richer than reward-chasing.","snippet":"Action driven by craving is far below the steadiness of clear discernment. Seek refuge in clear discernment, for those who chase results …","tags":["buddhi-yoga","result-attachment","clarity","krishna-arjuna","sattva"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":50,"order":97,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear action frees you from the weight of both success and failure.","snippet":"One who is united with clear discernment casts off both good and bad deeds in this life. Therefore, devote yourself to yoga, for yoga is …","tags":["buddhi-yoga","samatva","karma-yoga","punya-papa","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":51,"order":98,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom comes when action is done without clutching its reward.","snippet":"Wise people, united in clarity, abandon the fruit born of action and reach the flawless state, free from the bondage of birth.","tags":["karma-phala","buddhi-yoga","vairagya","birth-bondage","nishkama-karma"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":52,"order":99,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing ends the pull of future pleasures.","snippet":"When your intellect crosses the swamp of delusion, you will grow dispassionate toward what has been heard and what remains to be heard.","tags":["mohakalila","buddhi","nirveda","vairagya","sense-pleasures"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":53,"order":100,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Yoga begins when the mind stops being pulled in every direction.","snippet":"When your intellect, unmoved by conflicting teachings, becomes steady in complete stillness, you will attain yoga.","tags":["buddhi","samadhi","nischala","manas","chitta"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":54,"order":101,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Steady wisdom must be recognizable in ordinary movement.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Kesava, what are the marks of one whose wisdom is steady and who is absorbed in stillness? How does a person of steady und…","tags":["sthitaprajna","steady-mind","inquiry","equanimity","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":55,"order":102,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness begins when desire no longer defines your sense of enough.","snippet":"The divine said: When a person gives up all desires that arise in the mind, and is satisfied in the true self by the true self alone, tha…","tags":["sthitaprajna","kama","contentment","manas","atma"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":56,"order":103,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness remains when pleasure and pain lose their grip.","snippet":"The steady-minded sage is unshaken by sorrow, free from craving in joy, and beyond attachment, fear, and anger.","tags":["equanimity","sattva","attachment","fear","anger"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":57,"order":104,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady wisdom does not need life to feel favorable.","snippet":"One who feels no clinging anywhere, and neither rejoices nor hates when good or bad comes, has steady wisdom.","tags":["equanimity","anabhisneha","shubhashubha","pragya","steady-mind"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":58,"order":105,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness begins when the senses stop running outward.","snippet":"When this one draws the senses fully back from sense-objects, like a tortoise withdrawing its limbs, wisdom is steady.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","sense-withdrawal","tortoise-metaphor","steady-wisdom","pragya"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":59,"order":106,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Craving ends only when a higher reality becomes more compelling.","snippet":"Objects fall away from the self-denying person, but the taste for them remains. For the one who has seen the supreme reality, even that t…","tags":["vairagya","indriya","rasavarga","sense-restraint","sthitaprajna"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":60,"order":107,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Restraint fails without disciplined senses.","snippet":"Even for a wise person who strives, the turbulent senses can forcibly carry away the mind.","tags":["indriya","manas","sense-control","self-mastery","restlessness"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":61,"order":108,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Wisdom becomes steady only when the senses are no longer in charge.","snippet":"Having restrained all the senses, the disciplined one should sit devoted to Me. For one whose senses are under control, wisdom is firmly …","tags":["indriya-samyama","pragya","sense-control","inner-discipline","mind-stability"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":62,"order":109,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you dwell on becomes what you cling to, then what burns you.","snippet":"Thinking about sense objects creates attachment to them. Attachment gives rise to desire; desire gives rise to anger.","tags":["indriya","kama","krodha","sangha","manas"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":63,"order":110,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Anger first distorts seeing, then destroys the mind that should guide action.","snippet":"From anger comes delusion; from delusion, confusion of memory; from confusion of memory, loss of discernment; from loss of discernment, r…","tags":["krodha","smrti","buddhi","delusion","self-control"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":64,"order":111,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom comes from meeting experience without attraction or aversion.","snippet":"The disciplined person, moving among objects with senses under control and free from attraction and aversion, attains serenity.","tags":["raga","dvesha","indriya-nigraha","prasada","sankhya-yoga"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":65,"order":112,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing ends suffering and lets understanding settle at once.","snippet":"In inner clarity, all suffering falls away. For one whose mind is clear, understanding settles quickly.","tags":["prasada","buddhi","manas","equanimity","mental-clarity"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":66,"order":113,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Without inner discipline, even happiness has no place to stand.","snippet":"A restless mind has no steady discernment, no steady purpose, no peace, and without peace, no happiness.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","buddhi","shanti","manas","samyama"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":67,"order":114,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"One uncontrolled sense can carry the mind away.","snippet":"As the winds carry a boat on water, even one roaming sense can sweep away the mind\'s discernment.","tags":["indriya","manas","buddhi","sense-control","attention"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":68,"order":115,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady wisdom begins when the senses stop ruling your attention.","snippet":"Therefore, O mighty-armed one, the wisdom of one whose senses are fully restrained from sense-objects is steady.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","steady-intellect","sense-restraint","pragya","self-mastery"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":69,"order":116,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What the many pursue in sleep, the wise leave behind awake.","snippet":"What is night for all beings is wakefulness for the self-controlled one. What all beings wake toward is night for the seer who knows the …","tags":["indriya-samyama","vairagya","muni","desire","worldly-attachment"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":70,"order":117,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Peace belongs to the one who stays steady while desire moves.","snippet":"As rivers flow into the sea and the sea remains steady, so desires may enter a disciplined person without disturbing inner peace. The per…","tags":["samudra","kama","vairagya","equanimity","sense-restraint"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":71,"order":118,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Peace begins when wanting, owning, and self-importance fall away.","snippet":"One who gives up all desires, moves without craving, without possessiveness, and without ego, attains peace.","tags":["vairagya","nishkama","ahamkara","mamatva","shanti"]},{"chapter":2,"verse":72,"order":119,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness in the supreme reality ends confusion, even at life’s edge.","snippet":"Arjuna, this is the Brahmic state. Having reached it, one is never deluded. Remaining established in it even at the end of life, one atta…","tags":["brahmi-sthiti","brahmanirvana","equanimity","delusion","death-awareness"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":1,"order":120,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Mixed guidance deepens paralysis; clarity must come before action.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Janardana, if you consider understanding superior to action, then why do you urge me to this terrible action, O Keshava? Y…","tags":["arjuna-doubt","karma-vs-buddhi","clarity-seeking","chapter-3","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":2,"order":121,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Confusion ends when the mind asks for one clear direction.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Your words seem mixed and confusing to me. Tell me one thing clearly, so I may find the highest good.","tags":["arjuna-doubt","mixed-teaching","clear-guidance","kurukshetra","chapter-3"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":3,"order":122,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Different natures are steadied by different disciplines.","snippet":"The divine said: In this world, I have already taught two kinds of steadfast practice: the path of knowledge for the contemplative, and t…","tags":["karma-yoga","jnana-yoga","nishtha","sankhya","temperament"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":4,"order":123,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom is not found by escaping action, but by changing your relation to it.","snippet":"A person does not reach actionless freedom by avoiding action, nor by renouncing action alone does one reach perfection.","tags":["karmayoga","sannyasa","nishkama","renunciation","actionlessness"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":5,"order":124,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Inaction is an illusion; nature is already moving you.","snippet":"No one can remain without action even for a moment. Everyone is driven to act by the qualities born of nature.","tags":["prakriti","gunas","karma-yoga","inaction","agency"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":6,"order":125,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Outer restraint means nothing if the mind still feeds desire.","snippet":"One who restrains the organs of action but keeps thinking of sense objects in the mind is deluded and called a hypocrite.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","manas","hypocrisy","karma-yoga","desire"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":7,"order":126,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Self-mastery makes action noble, not the outer task alone.","snippet":"Arjuna, the one who restrains the senses with the mind and begins karma yoga without attachment is श्रेष्ठ.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","karma-yoga","asakti","manas","senses-control"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":8,"order":127,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action is unavoidable; even survival depends on it.","snippet":"Do the duty prescribed for you. Action is better than inaction, and even your body cannot be sustained by inaction.","tags":["karma yoga","niyata karma","duty","inaction","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":9,"order":128,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Work becomes bondage when it is done for yourself.","snippet":"Actions done for sacrifice free a person; actions done for personal gain bind. Therefore, Arjuna, do your duty without attachment for tha…","tags":["karma-yoga","nishkama","yajna","attachment","duty"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":10,"order":129,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Life flourishes when duty becomes mutual support.","snippet":"In the beginning, Prajapati created beings together with sacrifice and said: “By this, you shall prosper. May this sacrifice be the wish-…","tags":["yajna","prajapati","mutual-support","dharma","shared-duty"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":11,"order":130,"speaker":"Unknown","essence":"Your duty nourishes the whole, and the whole nourishes you back.","snippet":"By nurturing the radiant beings through this duty, let them nurture you. Nurturing one another, you will attain the highest good.","tags":["yajna","lokasangraha","mutuality","deva","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":12,"order":131,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is received must be offered back, or it becomes theft.","snippet":"The radiant beings, nourished by sacrifice, will give you the enjoyments you need. One who enjoys their gifts without offering back is a …","tags":["yajna","shared-duty","reciprocity","resource-use","theft"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":13,"order":132,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is offered purifies; what is hoarded for the self corrupts.","snippet":"Those who eat the leftovers of sacrifice are freed from all faults. Those who cook only for themselves eat only wrongdoing.","tags":["yajna","selflessness","offering","karmic-purity","egoism"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":14,"order":133,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action sustains the cycle that makes life possible.","snippet":"All beings arise from food. Food comes from rain. Rain comes from sacrifice. Sacrifice arises from action.","tags":["yajna","anna","parjanya","karma","sustenance"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":15,"order":134,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action is not random; it rests in a deeper, sustaining order.","snippet":"Know that action comes from the Vedas, and the Vedas come from the imperishable. Therefore, the all-pervading supreme reality is always e…","tags":["yajna","karma-yoga","veda","akshara","cosmic-order"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":16,"order":135,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A life detached from duty empties itself from within.","snippet":"O Partha, the one who does not follow this cycle set in motion here lives in vain, delighting only in the senses and living a life of wro…","tags":["karma-yoga","yajna","indriya-sukha","dharma","cycle-of-action"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":17,"order":136,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Fulfillment in the true self ends the need for striving.","snippet":"The person who delights in the true self, is satisfied in the true self, and is content in the true self has no duty left.","tags":["atma-rati","atma-trupta","santushta","karma-yoga","inner-fulfillment"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":18,"order":137,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom ends the need to profit from action.","snippet":"For the perfected person, no purpose remains in doing, and no purpose remains in not doing. No being in the world is a source of personal…","tags":["nishkama-karma","karma-yoga","vairagya","action-without-gain","selfless-action"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":19,"order":138,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom comes when action is done without grasping at its reward.","snippet":"Therefore, always perform your duty without attachment; by acting without attachment, a person reaches the supreme.","tags":["nishkama karma","attachment","duty","kurukshetra","karma yoga"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":20,"order":139,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Perfection comes through action that serves more than the self.","snippet":"Janaka and others attained perfection through action itself. You should act too, while keeping the welfare of the world in view.","tags":["janaka","lokasangraha","nishkama-karma","karma-yoga","duty"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":21,"order":140,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest standard is not spoken; it is copied.","snippet":"Whatever the best person does, others follow. Whatever standard they set, the world copies.","tags":["role-model","public-example","conduct","social-influence","maryada"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":22,"order":141,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even the fulfilled keep working, because action need not come from lack.","snippet":"O Partha, there is nothing in the three worlds that I must do, and nothing I have not yet gained that must be gained. Yet I remain engage…","tags":["karma-yoga","lokasangraha","krishna-example","action-without-need","duty"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":23,"order":142,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Careless withdrawal by the highest would unravel everyone below.","snippet":"For if I ever stopped acting with care, people would follow my path in every way, Arjuna.","tags":["role-modeling","loka-sangraha","karma-yoga","social-order","duty"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":24,"order":143,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even the highest must act to prevent disorder.","snippet":"If I did not act, these worlds would fall into ruin. I would create disorder and destroy these people.","tags":["lokasangraha","duty","karma-yoga","social-order","responsibility"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":25,"order":144,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Wisdom keeps acting, but never for personal gain.","snippet":"As the ignorant act with attachment to action, so should the wise act without attachment, seeking the welfare of the world.","tags":["lokasangraha","karmayoga","asakti","wise-action","role-model"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":26,"order":145,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Wisdom should steady people, not shake their footing.","snippet":"An awakened person should not unsettle the minds of those attached to action. Instead, acting skillfully, such a person should engage the…","tags":["lokasangraha","buddhibheda","karma-sanga","wise conduct","guided action"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":27,"order":146,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The doer is imagined; action belongs to nature\'s forces.","snippet":"All actions are carried out in every way by the qualities of nature. Deluded by ego, a person thinks, \'I am the doer.\'","tags":["prakriti","gunas","ahamkara","kartahamhiti","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":28,"order":147,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing action as nature\'s movement ends attachment.","snippet":"The one who truly understands the division of qualities and actions does not cling, seeing that qualities act upon qualities.","tags":["gunas","karma-yoga","vairagya","ahankara","kartabhava"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":29,"order":148,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clarity should guide confusion, not crush it.","snippet":"The ignorant, deluded by the qualities of nature, cling to actions born of those qualities. The wise should not unsettle those who do not…","tags":["gunas","delusion","instruction","karma-yoga","gentle-guidance"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":30,"order":149,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action becomes free when you stop claiming its results.","snippet":"Surrender all actions to me with the disciplined mind. Free from desire, possessiveness, and sorrow, fight.","tags":["nishkama-karma","karma-yoga","vairagya","mamata","yuddha"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":31,"order":150,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Trusting the teaching frees action from its binding force.","snippet":"Those who always follow this teaching of Mine with trust and without fault-finding are freed from the bonds of action.","tags":["shraddha","anasuya","karma-bandha","action-without-attachment","krishna-teaching"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":32,"order":151,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Rejecting clear guidance leaves the mind stranded.","snippet":"But those who, finding fault with this teaching, do not follow it—know them to be deluded in all knowledge and ruined in understanding.","tags":["karma-yoga","shraddha","abhyasuya","mental-confusion","discipline"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":33,"order":152,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Nature drives behavior; force alone cannot overrule it.","snippet":"Even the wise act according to their own nature. All beings follow nature; what can restraint do?","tags":["prakriti","gunas","self-mastery","habit","restraint"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":34,"order":153,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when attraction and aversion stop steering action.","snippet":"Attachment and aversion sit in every sense-object. Do not come under their power, for they are your enemies on the path.","tags":["indriya","raga-dvesha","sense-control","karma-yoga","self-mastery"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":35,"order":154,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Imperfect right action is safer than perfect imitation.","snippet":"Better is one\'s own duty, though imperfect, than another\'s duty well performed. Better death in one\'s own duty; another\'s duty is dangerous.","tags":["svadharma","paradharma","role-fidelity","duty","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":36,"order":155,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Compulsion has a cause, and Arjuna wants to name it.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O descendant of the Vrishni clan, what drives a person to commit wrongdoing, even unwillingly, as if forced?","tags":["inner conflict","compulsion","arjuna-question","moral struggle","rajas"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":37,"order":156,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire is not harmless; it mutates into the force that ruins judgment.","snippet":"Krishna said: Desire, born of rajas, turns into anger. It is all-consuming and deeply destructive. Know it as your enemy here.","tags":["rajas","kama","krodha","inner-enemy","discernment"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":38,"order":157,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing is not destroyed; it is simply covered.","snippet":"As fire is covered by smoke, a mirror by dust, and a womb by a membrane, so clear seeing is covered by desire.","tags":["kama","viveka","avidya","rajas","inner-veiling"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":39,"order":158,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire does not just tempt; it hides wisdom itself.","snippet":"O son of Kunti, wisdom is covered by this desire, the eternal enemy of the wise, as fire is never satisfied.","tags":["kama","buddhi","avidya","inner conflict","desire"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":40,"order":159,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire conquers by hijacking the mind\'s own instruments.","snippet":"The senses, the mind, and the discerning mind are said to be its seat. Through them, it deludes the embodied person by veiling understand…","tags":["kama","indriya","manas","buddhi","self-mastery"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":41,"order":160,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sense-control comes before clear action.","snippet":"Therefore, O best of the Bharatas, first control the senses, and then destroy this great sinner, the destroyer of knowledge and wisdom.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","kama","self-restraint","impulse-control","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":42,"order":161,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire sits above reason, so mastery must begin earlier.","snippet":"The senses are higher than the body; the mind is higher than the senses; the discerning mind is higher than the mind. What is beyond the …","tags":["indriya","manas","buddhi","kama","self-mastery"]},{"chapter":3,"verse":43,"order":162,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire loses power when the higher mind takes command.","snippet":"Thus, knowing the higher beyond the intellect, steady the lower self by the higher self, and destroy that enemy in the form of desire, wh…","tags":["kama","buddhi","indriya","manas","self-mastery"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":1,"order":163,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Timeless wisdom survives by being passed on, not newly invented.","snippet":"The Lord said: I taught this imperishable yoga to Vivasvan. Vivasvan taught it to Manu, and Manu taught it to Ikshvaku.","tags":["parampara","avyaya-yoga","vivasvan","manu","ikshvaku"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":2,"order":164,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even timeless wisdom disappears when no one keeps receiving it.","snippet":"O scorcher of foes, this yoga was known by the royal sages through an unbroken lineage. In the course of great time, this yoga was lost i…","tags":["parampara","rajarshi","lost-yoga","lineage","jnana-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":3,"order":165,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deepest teaching opens only to devotion and trust.","snippet":"Because you are my devotee and my friend, I have taught you today this ancient yoga. It is a supreme secret.","tags":["parapara","rahasya","bhakta","sakhya","jnana-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":4,"order":166,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Doubt becomes the doorway to deeper seeing.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Your birth is recent, while the birth of the Sun is ancient. How am I to understand that you taught this yoga at the beginni…","tags":["arjuna","inquiry","time","vivasvan","jnana-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":5,"order":167,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your memory is partial; the divine awareness is not.","snippet":"Krishna said: Many births of yours and mine have passed, Arjuna. I know them all, but you do not, enemy-burner.","tags":["janma","smriti","krishna","arjuna","timelessness"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":6,"order":168,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The unborn can still appear without ceasing to be free.","snippet":"Though unborn and imperishable, and though I am the lord of all beings, I manifest myself by controlling my own nature through my own pow…","tags":["avatar","janma","prakriti","yogamaya","krishna-incarnation"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":7,"order":169,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"When dharma collapses, the divine steps into history.","snippet":"Whenever there is a decline of dharma and a rise of adharma, I manifest myself.","tags":["avatara","dharma","adharma","krishna-manifestation","cosmic-order"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":8,"order":170,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine returns whenever order must be restored.","snippet":"For the protection of the righteous, for the destruction of wrongdoers, and for the establishment of dharma, I appear age after age.","tags":["avatar","dharma-restoration","krishna-incarnation","adharma","yuga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":9,"order":171,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing Krishna truly ends the cycle of return.","snippet":"Arjuna, my birth and action are divine. One who truly understands this does not take birth again after leaving the body, but comes to me.","tags":["avatar","divine-incarnation","janma-karma","moksha","krishna-identity"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":10,"order":172,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Purified minds reach what fear and craving cannot.","snippet":"Many, purified by the austerity of knowledge, free from attachment, fear, and anger, absorbed in Me and taking refuge in Me, have attaine…","tags":["vairagya","bhava","knowledge-austerity","fearlessness","inner-purification"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":11,"order":173,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine response matches the way you come forward.","snippet":"As people approach Me, so I respond to them. All people follow My path in every way, O Arjuna.","tags":["prapatti","bhajana","anugraha","shraddha","bhakti"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":12,"order":174,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire for quick success makes people chase fast-acting powers.","snippet":"People who want quick success worship radiant beings, because results from action come quickly in the human world.","tags":["karmaphala","devata-upasana","quick-results","artha","ritual-seeking"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":13,"order":175,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The source of order stands outside the order it creates.","snippet":"The four social orders were created by Me according to qualities and actions. Though I am their maker, know Me as the unchanging non-doer.","tags":["varna","guna","karma","akarta","avyaya"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":14,"order":176,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowing the action is not yours to possess breaks its grip.","snippet":"Actions do not stain me, and I do not crave their fruits. One who knows me this way is not bound by actions.","tags":["karma-phala","akartā","nishkama","action-without-attachment","krishna-identity"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":15,"order":177,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action is the path even for those seeking freedom.","snippet":"Even seekers of freedom acted after knowing this. Therefore, do the work that your ancestors always did.","tags":["mumukshu","ancient-duty","krishna-instruction","karma-yoga","rightful-action"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":16,"order":178,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing about action is what breaks bondage.","snippet":"What is action, and what is inaction? Even the wise are confused here. I will explain that action to you, knowing which you will be freed…","tags":["karma-tattva","akarma","vikarma","jnana-yoga","moksha"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":17,"order":179,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action cannot be judged quickly; its true pattern is subtle.","snippet":"Action, forbidden action, and inaction must all be understood, because the movement of action is hard to grasp.","tags":["karmano gati","vikarma","akarma","discrimination","jnana yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":18,"order":180,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom can live inside action, and bondage can hide inside stillness.","snippet":"One who sees action in inaction, and inaction in action, is wise among people; that person is disciplined and complete in action.","tags":["karmanyakarma","akarma","jnana-yoga","inner freedom","actionless action"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":19,"order":181,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowledge frees action from craving and leaves no binding trace.","snippet":"The wise call that person learned whose actions begin without desire or personal planning, and whose deeds are burned by the fire of know…","tags":["jnana-agni","kamasankalpa","karma-burnt","pandita","detached-action"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":20,"order":182,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action loses its grip when nothing in you waits to possess its fruit.","snippet":"One who has abandoned attachment to the fruits of action, remains ever content, and depends on nothing, does nothing at all even while fu…","tags":["karma-phala","anashakti","nityatripta","nirashraya","nishkama-karma"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":21,"order":183,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom from clinging keeps action untouched.","snippet":"One who has no hope, who has controlled the body and mind, and who has given up all possessions, does only bodily action and incurs no fa…","tags":["nishkama","aparigraha","karma-yoga","self-mastery","action-without-clinging"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":22,"order":184,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equal-minded action leaves no hook for bondage.","snippet":"Content with whatever comes by itself, beyond opposites, free from envy, equal in success and failure, such a person is not bound even wh…","tags":["karma-yoga","vairagya","samatva","envy","success-failure"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":23,"order":185,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action loses its grip when it becomes offering, not possession.","snippet":"For one who has given up attachment, is freed, and whose mind rests in knowledge, all action melts away when done only for sacrifice.","tags":["nishkama-karma","yajna","attachment","jnaana","karma-phala"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":24,"order":186,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"When action is fully absorbed, even the result is not separate from Brahman.","snippet":"In such sacrifice, the offering is Brahman, the oblation is Brahman, and the act of offering into the fire of Brahman is Brahman. One who…","tags":["brahman","yajna","karma-samadhi","nonduality","offering"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":25,"order":187,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sacrifice changes shape, but its aim remains surrender into the absolute.","snippet":"Some yogis offer sacrifice to the divine alone. Others offer the self into the fire of Brahman through sacrifice itself.","tags":["yajna","brahmagni","offering","karma-yoga","jnana-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":26,"order":188,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Restraint can consume desire before desire consumes you.","snippet":"Some yogis offer the senses into the fires of restraint. Others offer sound and the other sense-objects into the fires of the senses.","tags":["indriya","samyama","sense-restraint","yajna","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":27,"order":189,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowledge turns self-control into a fire that consumes every impulse.","snippet":"Others offer all the activities of the senses and the life-force into the fire of self-control, lit by knowledge.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","prana","atma-samyama","jnana","homa"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":28,"order":190,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sacrifice can be wealth, effort, austerity, or study.","snippet":"Others offer wealth, austerity, yoga, and the study of sacred texts as sacrifice, while disciplined seekers make these offerings with fir…","tags":["svadhyaya","tapas","yajna","discipline","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":29,"order":191,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Breath itself can become disciplined offering.","snippet":"Some offer the outgoing breath into the incoming breath, and the incoming breath into the outgoing breath, restraining the movement of bo…","tags":["pranayama","yajna","regulated-eating","breath-control","tapas"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":30,"order":192,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Discipline itself becomes offering, and offering burns away inner stain.","snippet":"Some offer the breath into the breath through regulated breathing; some, with regulated food, offer the life-forces into the life-forces.…","tags":["pranayama","yajna","regulated-diet","self-discipline","purification"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":31,"order":193,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A life without offering cannot even support itself.","snippet":"Those who partake of the nectar left over from sacrifice attain the eternal supreme reality. This world is not for the one who does not p…","tags":["yajna","anna-prasada","reciprocity","karma-yoga","sacrifice"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":32,"order":194,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing every offering as action frees you from action’s binding force.","snippet":"In this way, many kinds of sacrifice are described in the sacred teaching. Know them all as born of action; knowing this, you will be fre…","tags":["yajna","karmaja","brahmano-mukhe","moksha","ritual-action"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":33,"order":195,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowledge is the point where every action finally comes to rest.","snippet":"O Arjuna, knowledge-sacrifice is better than sacrifice made of material things. All action and all matter end in knowledge.","tags":["jnana-yajna","karma","vidya","ritual","understanding"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":34,"order":196,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Humility opens the door to knowledge that pride cannot reach.","snippet":"Know that by prostration, by sincere questioning, and by service. The wise who see reality will teach you that knowledge.","tags":["pariprashna","seva","tattvadarshi","jnana","guru"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":35,"order":197,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowing deeply ends confusion by revealing one reality in all beings.","snippet":"Knowing which, you will not fall into confusion again. Through which, you will see all beings without remainder first in yourself, and th…","tags":["jnana","moha","sarvabhuta","advaita","atma-darshana"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":36,"order":198,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear understanding can carry even the heaviest past across.","snippet":"Even if you are the worst of wrongdoers, you will cross all wrongdoing by the raft of knowledge alone.","tags":["jnana","papa","papa-krita","knowledge","transformation"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":37,"order":199,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real understanding burns the binding power of every action.","snippet":"As a blazing fire reduces fuel to ashes, so the fire of knowledge reduces all actions to ashes, Arjuna.","tags":["jnana-agni","karma-burn","knowledge-fire","ch4","moksha-through-knowledge"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":38,"order":200,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Nothing purifies like knowledge, and yoga ripens it from within.","snippet":"No purifier compares to knowledge in this world. The one perfected in yoga finds that knowledge within the self in time.","tags":["jnana","yoga-siddhi","purification","atma-jnana","self-realization"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":39,"order":201,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Trust, discipline, and restraint make room for peace.","snippet":"The person with trust, discipline, and controlled senses gains knowledge. Having gained knowledge, that person quickly reaches supreme pe…","tags":["shraddha","indriya-nigraha","jnana","shanti","sadhana"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":40,"order":202,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A divided mind loses both peace and direction.","snippet":"The ignorant and faithless person who doubts is ruined. For the doubter, there is neither this world, nor the next, nor happiness.","tags":["samsaya","shraddha","viveka","mental-fragmentation","jnana-yoga"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":41,"order":203,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when action no longer leaves a hook.","snippet":"O Dhananjaya, actions do not bind the one who has renounced action through yoga, whose doubts have been cut away by knowledge, and who ab…","tags":["jnana-yoga","karma-bandha","yogasannyasta","sanshaya","atma-vanta"]},{"chapter":4,"verse":42,"order":204,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowledge cuts doubt, and then action becomes possible again.","snippet":"Therefore, O Bharata, cut away this doubt in your heart, born of ignorance, with the sword of knowledge. Stand in yoga and rise up for ba…","tags":["doubt","ignorance","clear seeing","kurukshetra","action after insight"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":1,"order":205,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Choose the path that truly serves your welfare.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Krishna, you praise both renunciation of action and yoga of action. Tell me clearly which one is definitely better for my we…","tags":["renunciation","karmayoga","arjuna","chapter5","inquiry"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":2,"order":206,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Renunciation matures when action continues without grasping.","snippet":"Renunciation and karma yoga both lead to the highest good, but karma yoga is better than renouncing action.","tags":["karma yoga","sannyasa","nishkama","action without attachment","renunciation"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":3,"order":207,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom comes when craving and resistance no longer steer the mind.","snippet":"One who neither hates nor desires is always a renunciant. Free from opposites, such a person is easily released from bondage, O mighty-ar…","tags":["vairagya","karma-sannyasa","dvesha","kanksha","dvandva"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":4,"order":208,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Different methods can reach the same fulfillment when practiced wholeheartedly.","snippet":"The unwise say that renunciation and yoga lead to different results. The wise see that one who is firmly established in either reaches th…","tags":["sankhya","karma-yoga","renunciation","fruit-of-action","dual-path"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":5,"order":209,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Different paths can lead to the same freedom.","snippet":"The state reached by the wise is also reached through yoga. One who sees wisdom and yoga as one sees rightly.","tags":["sankhya","karma-yoga","nonduality","equivalence","renunciation"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":6,"order":210,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real renunciation grows through practice, not withdrawal.","snippet":"But, mighty-armed one, renunciation without yoga is hard to attain. The disciplined seeker in yoga quickly reaches the supreme reality.","tags":["karma-sannyasa","renunciation","yoga","brahman","muni"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":7,"order":211,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Inner freedom lets action happen without leaving a trace.","snippet":"A disciplined yogi, pure in mind, self-mastered, and senses conquered, sees the same self in all beings and is not tainted by action whil…","tags":["karma-sannyasa","jितendriya","manas-shuddhi","samyama","nonattachment"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":8,"order":212,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing life happen is not the same as claiming it.","snippet":"The knower of reality should think, \\"I do nothing at all,\\" while seeing, hearing, touching, smelling, eating, walking, taking, speaking, …","tags":["doership","indriyas","sankhya","witness-consciousness","karma-sannyasa"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":9,"order":213,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action happens; ownership is the illusion.","snippet":"Even while speaking, releasing, taking, opening, and closing the eyes, the wise know: the senses move among their objects.","tags":["indriya","sense-objects","kartṛtva","non-doership","vairagya"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":10,"order":214,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action without attachment leaves no stain.","snippet":"One who offers actions to Brahman, renounces attachment, and acts is not stained by wrongdoing, just as a lotus leaf is untouched by water.","tags":["nishkama-karma","vairagya","lotus-leaf","attachment","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":11,"order":215,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action becomes cleansing when attachment is removed.","snippet":"Yogis perform action with body, mind, intellect, and the senses, giving up attachment, only for inner purification.","tags":["karma-yoga","attachment","inner-purification","senses","action-without-clinging"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":12,"order":216,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Peace comes when action is no longer chained to reward.","snippet":"The disciplined one gives up the fruit of action and attains steady peace. The undisciplined one, clinging to results through desire, bec…","tags":["karmaphala","nishkama","attachment","steady-peace","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":13,"order":217,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when action no longer feels personally owned.","snippet":"The embodied one, who has mastered the senses and mind, dwells happily in the city of nine gates, mentally renouncing all actions, neithe…","tags":["doership","karma-sannyasa","nine-gate-body","mental-renunciation","vairagya"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":14,"order":218,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What looks like personal control is nature moving through form.","snippet":"The supreme being creates neither doership nor actions nor the link between action and result for people. Nature alone keeps moving.","tags":["doership","svabhava","karma-phala","prakriti","karta-bhava"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":15,"order":219,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ignorance, not action, is what keeps beings confused.","snippet":"The all-pervading one takes neither anyone\'s wrongdoing nor anyone\'s good deed. Knowledge is covered by ignorance, and that is why living…","tags":["avidya","karma-phala","jnana","delusion","witness"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":16,"order":220,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing does not create reality; it uncovers what was always there.","snippet":"But for those whose ignorance has been destroyed by knowledge of the true self, that knowledge reveals the supreme reality like the sun.","tags":["avidya","vidya","clarity","atmajnana","paramatman"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":17,"order":221,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Complete alignment with the supreme reality ends the cycle of return.","snippet":"Those whose intellect is fixed in That, whose mind is That, who are established in That, and who are devoted to That, go to the state of …","tags":["apunaravritti","tadbuddhi","tatparayana","jnana","moksha"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":18,"order":222,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real wisdom erases rank and reveals sameness.","snippet":"The wise see the same reality in a learned, humble brahmin, a cow, an elephant, a dog, and an outcaste.","tags":["samadarsina","equal-vision","brahmana","chandal","nonduality"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":19,"order":223,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sameness of mind is the real conquest; everything else is aftermath.","snippet":"Those whose mind rests in sameness conquer rebirth here itself. The supreme reality is flawless and equal, so they are established in it.","tags":["samatva","brahman","rebirth","equanimity","inner steadiness"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":20,"order":224,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness begins when pleasure and pain lose their power over you.","snippet":"One who does not rejoice at the pleasant, and does not shrink from the unpleasant, is steady in understanding, free from delusion, and es…","tags":["samatva","sthita-prajna","buddhi","brahmavid","pleasant-unpleasant"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":21,"order":225,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when outer contact stops controlling inner joy.","snippet":"One who is not attached to outer contacts finds the joy within the true self. Unified with the supreme reality, that person enjoys unendi…","tags":["vairagya","indriya-sparsha","brahma-yoga","inner-joy","imperishable-happiness"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":22,"order":226,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Passing pleasure loses its power when its ending is seen.","snippet":"The pleasures born from contact with the senses are only sources of suffering. They have a beginning and an end, O Arjuna, and the wise d…","tags":["indriya","vishaya","bhoga","vairagya","duhkha"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":23,"order":227,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Master the surge before it masters you.","snippet":"Whoever can withstand the surge of desire and anger here before the body falls, is a disciplined person and is truly happy.","tags":["kama","krodha","sense-control","self-mastery","inner-restraint"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":24,"order":228,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Inner fulfillment makes freedom possible right now.","snippet":"One who finds happiness within, delights within, and has inner light alone, becomes one with the supreme reality and reaches freedom in t…","tags":["brahmanirvana","antarjyoti","inner-contentment","vairagya","samadhi"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":25,"order":229,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom arrives when doubt ends and life turns toward all beings.","snippet":"Sages who are free of impurity, free of doubt, self-controlled, and devoted to the welfare of all beings attain freedom in the supreme re…","tags":["bhramनिर्वाण","doubt","self-control","sarvabhutahita","sage"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":26,"order":230,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom comes when desire and anger no longer govern the mind.","snippet":"For those free from desire and anger, with disciplined minds and self-knowledge, freedom in the supreme reality is near on both sides.","tags":["kama","krodha","yati","yatacetas","brahmanirvana"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":27,"order":231,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Outer restraint and balanced breath prepare the mind for freedom.","snippet":"Leaving outer objects outside, fixing the gaze between the eyebrows, and balancing the inward and outward breaths moving through the nose.","tags":["pranayama","sense-withdrawal","brahmacharya","meditation","mind-control"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":28,"order":232,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins where desire, fear, and anger lose authority.","snippet":"One who has controlled the senses, mind, and intellect, who seeks freedom as the highest aim, and who is free from desire, fear, and ange…","tags":["indriya-nigraha","manas","buddhi","vairagya","moksha"]},{"chapter":5,"verse":29,"order":233,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Peace comes from knowing the divine receives all effort and cares for all beings.","snippet":"Knowing me as the enjoyer of all sacrifice and austerity, the great lord of all worlds, and the friend of all beings, one attains peace.","tags":["yajna","tapas","suhrit","ishvara","peace"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":1,"order":234,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Renunciation means acting without needing to own the result.","snippet":"One who performs the required action without taking shelter in the fruit of action is a renunciate and a yogi. Not one who merely gives u…","tags":["nishkama-karma","sannyasa","yoga","karma-phala","renunciation"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":2,"order":235,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Yoga begins when the mind stops clutching its own agenda.","snippet":"Arjuna, what people call renunciation is yoga. No one becomes a yogi without giving up intentions.","tags":["sankalpa","sannyasa","raja-yoga","vairagya","manas"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":3,"order":236,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"You reach steadiness through action, then preserve it through stillness.","snippet":"For the sage who seeks to rise into yoga, action is the means. For the one who has risen in yoga, stillness is the means.","tags":["dhyana","shama","arurukshu","yogarudha","meditation-discipline"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":4,"order":237,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Yoga begins when neither pleasure nor action can hook you.","snippet":"When one no longer clings to sense pleasures or to actions, that person is called established in yoga, having renounced all intentions.","tags":["dhyana","vairagya","indriya","sankalpa","yogarudha"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":5,"order":238,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your own inner handling makes you rise or collapse.","snippet":"Lift yourself by yourself; do not let yourself fall. The true self is its own friend, and the true self is its own enemy.","tags":["self-mastery","dhyana-yoga","manas","discipline","inner-conflict"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":6,"order":239,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The same inner nature that frees you can also fight you.","snippet":"For one who has conquered the lower self by the true self, the true self is a friend. For one who has not conquered the lower self, the t…","tags":["atma","self-mastery","manas","inner-conflict","dhyana-yoga"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":7,"order":240,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness makes the highest reality feel near in every opposite.","snippet":"For one who has conquered the self and is serene, the supreme reality is ever present in heat and cold, pleasure and pain, honor and dish…","tags":["dhyana-yoga","jitatma","prashanta","samatva","manapaman"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":8,"order":241,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True mastery makes gold and dust feel identical.","snippet":"One whose mind is satisfied by knowledge and realization, who remains steady, who has conquered the senses, and who sees clay, stone, and…","tags":["samabuddhi","indriya-jaya","kutastha","vairagya","dhyana"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":9,"order":242,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equal vision toward all people marks the highest steadiness.","snippet":"The one whose understanding is equal toward friend, enemy, neutral person, mediator, hateful person, relative, the virtuous, and the sinf…","tags":["samabuddhi","equanimity","friend-enemy","meditation","bias"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":10,"order":243,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady inward practice begins when desire and possessiveness end.","snippet":"The disciplined yogi, dwelling alone in seclusion, should constantly unite the mind with the supreme being, free from desire and possessi…","tags":["dhyana","aparigraha","nirasha","yatatmya","seclusion"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":11,"order":244,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A steady mind begins with a steady seat.","snippet":"Having placed a firm seat for himself on a clean spot, neither too high nor too low, with cloth, deerskin, and kusha grass laid in layers.","tags":["dhyana","asana","meditation setup","kusha grass","seating"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":12,"order":245,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Meditation begins by gathering the mind and training the senses.","snippet":"Sitting on that seat, with the mind made one-pointed and the movements of mind and senses restrained, one should practice yoga for inner …","tags":["dhyana","ekagra","manas","indriya-nigraha","atma-shuddhi"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":13,"order":246,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady posture is the first gate to a steady mind.","snippet":"Holding the body, head, and neck straight and still, and gazing only at the tip of the nose without looking around.","tags":["dhyana","asana","mind-control","sense-withdrawal","meditation-posture"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":14,"order":247,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A disciplined mind can rest in devotion without fear.","snippet":"The yogi, with a peaceful mind, free of fear, and firm in celibate discipline, restrains the mind, fixes awareness on Me, and sits devote…","tags":["dhyana","brahmacharya","manas-samyama","fearlessness","meditative-discipline"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":15,"order":248,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A steady mind reaches the peace that restlessness can never touch.","snippet":"The disciplined yogi, always uniting the mind in this way, attains the supreme peace of freedom rooted in Me.","tags":["dhyana","manas","nirvana","yoga","mental-discipline"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":16,"order":249,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Balance makes meditation possible; extremes break it.","snippet":"Yoga is not for one who eats too much, nor for one who eats nothing at all. It is not for one who sleeps too much, nor for one who stays …","tags":["dhyana","moderation","sleep","ahara","discipline"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":17,"order":250,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Balanced living makes inner practice possible.","snippet":"Yoga that destroys suffering comes from balanced eating, balanced activity, balanced work, and balanced sleep and waking.","tags":["dhyana","moderation","sleep","ahara","vihara"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":18,"order":251,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Yoga begins when craving loses its grip and the mind comes home.","snippet":"When the controlled mind rests in the true self alone and is free from craving for all pleasures, that person is called united in yoga.","tags":["dhyana","manas","vairagya","chitta","atman"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":19,"order":252,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A trained mind becomes steady enough to stop flickering.","snippet":"As a lamp in a windless place does not flicker, so the disciplined mind of a yogi does not waver while practicing yoga of the true self.","tags":["dhyana","chitta","lamp-metaphor","mind-control","stillness"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":20,"order":253,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Stillness reveals a completeness that no outside thing can improve.","snippet":"When the restrained mind becomes still through yoga practice, and the person sees the true self by the true self, one is content in the t…","tags":["dhyana","chitta","uparama","atman-darshan","self-contentment"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":21,"order":254,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True joy is deeper than sensation and keeps you from wavering.","snippet":"One knows the boundless joy beyond the senses and grasped by the discerning mind; established in it, one never truly falls away.","tags":["dhyana","samadhi","buddhi","indriya","inner-joy"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":22,"order":255,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True fulfillment leaves nothing more to chase and nothing strong enough to unsettle you.","snippet":"Having attained it, one thinks no greater gain exists. Established in it, one is not shaken even by great sorrow.","tags":["dhyana","samadhi","chitta","vairagya","steadiness"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":23,"order":256,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Yoga is the breaking of suffering’s grip, practiced steadily.","snippet":"Know that as yoga: the severance of union with suffering. Practice that yoga with certainty, with an undiscouraged mind.","tags":["dhyana-yoga","meditation","duhkha","abhyasa","vairagya"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":24,"order":257,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire loses power when the mind stops feeding it.","snippet":"Abandon every desire born of resolve, and restrain the whole field of the senses on all sides with the mind alone.","tags":["kama","manas","indriya","dhyana","sense-restraint"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":25,"order":258,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Stillness comes by degrees when the mind stops feeding itself.","snippet":"Little by little, the mind should be quieted by steady discernment. Fix the mind in the true self and think of nothing else.","tags":["dhyana","manas","buddhi","atma-samstha","mental-restraint"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":26,"order":259,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The mind is mastered by repeated return, not by force.","snippet":"Whenever the restless, unsteady mind wanders, bring it back under the control of the true self.","tags":["dhyana","manas","restless-mind","self-mastery","meditation-practice"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":27,"order":260,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Joy comes when the restless mind finally becomes still.","snippet":"The yogi whose mind is peaceful, whose passion is stilled, and who is free from impurity attains the highest joy.","tags":["dhyana","manas","rajas","buddhi","samadhi"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":28,"order":261,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Repeated union with the supreme reality yields effortless, lasting joy.","snippet":"Thus, the disciplined yogi, free from impurity, always unites the self with the supreme reality and attains limitless joy through that co…","tags":["dhyana","brahmasparsha","manas","yogi","meditation"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":29,"order":262,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equal vision dissolves the illusion of separation.","snippet":"The one united in yoga sees the true self in all beings and all beings in the true self, seeing everything with equal vision.","tags":["samadarshana","dhyana","sarvabhutastha","yoga-yukta","advaita"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":30,"order":263,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing the divine everywhere ends separation.","snippet":"Who sees Me in all beings and sees all beings in Me, I am never lost to that person, and that person is never lost to Me.","tags":["sarvabhuta","ekatva","bhakti","dhyana","krishna-sarvatraga"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":31,"order":264,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Unity turns every action into abiding presence.","snippet":"The yogi who abides in unity and worships Me in all beings lives in Me, even while acting in every way.","tags":["ekatva","bhajana","sarvabhutasthita","devotional presence","meditation in action"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":32,"order":265,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equal vision makes you unshaken by pleasure or pain.","snippet":"O Arjuna, the yogi who sees all beings as equal through the measure of the true self, and sees pleasure and pain alike, is considered the…","tags":["samatva","dhyana","equanimity","sukha-duhkha","meditative-vision"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":33,"order":266,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Restlessness makes even clear teaching feel unreachable.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Krishna, you have described this yoga as balanced, but I do not see its steady practice, because the mind is restless.","tags":["manas","chitta","restlessness","arjuna-doubt","dhyana-yoga"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":34,"order":267,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The mind resists control like wind resists the hand.","snippet":"The mind is restless, turbulent, stubborn, and strong. I think controlling it is as hard as controlling the wind.","tags":["manas","dhyana","chanchala","self-mastery","meditation"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":35,"order":268,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A restless mind is not a verdict; it is a training ground.","snippet":"The mind is hard to control, but it is mastered through practice and detachment.","tags":["manas","abhyasa","vairagya","dhyana","mind-training"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":36,"order":269,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Yoga becomes reachable when the mind is trained, not merely hoped for.","snippet":"Yoga is hard to attain for one whose mind is not fully controlled. But for one who controls the mind and strives with the right method, i…","tags":["manas","vashyatma","abhyasa","vairagya","dhyana"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":37,"order":270,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Faith without completion still deserves a clear answer.","snippet":"Arjuna said: What happens to a person who has faith but lacks steady effort, whose mind turns away from yoga before full success is reach…","tags":["shraddha","sadhana","yoga-bhrashta","arjuna-prashna","dhyana-yoga"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":38,"order":271,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Half-finished striving can feel like total ruin.","snippet":"O mighty-armed one, does a person who has fallen from both sides, like a torn cloud, perish without support, deluded on the path of the s…","tags":["dhyana-yoga","arjuna-question","fallen-ascetic","brahma-patha","spiritual-fear"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":39,"order":272,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Only clear seeing can end confusion completely.","snippet":"O Krishna, only you can fully cut away this doubt. No one else is able to remove it.","tags":["samsaya","krishna","guidance","doubt","inquiry"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":40,"order":273,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sincere effort toward the good cannot end in ruin.","snippet":"Krishna said: O Partha, there is no destruction for him either here or hereafter. No one who does good ever comes to a bad end, my dear.","tags":["dhyana-yoga","sadhana","falling-short","punya","yogabhrashta"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":41,"order":274,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A fall from yoga still carries you forward.","snippet":"The one who falls from yoga reaches the worlds earned by good deeds, dwells there for many long years, and is then born again in the hous…","tags":["yogabhrashta","punyakrita","rebirth","sadhana","family-birth"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":42,"order":275,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A fallen practitioner is not lost; the next birth can restart the work.","snippet":"Or he is born into the family of wise yogis. Such a birth is very rare in this world.","tags":["yogabhraṣṭa","punyakarma","sadhana","rebirth","family-of-yogis"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":43,"order":276,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Nothing gained in sincere practice is ever truly lost.","snippet":"O son of Kuru, there he effortlessly regains the spiritual understanding from his previous life. Then he strives again, with greater forc…","tags":["yogabhraṣṭa","punyakarma","previous-life practice","buddhisamyooga","recovery of discipline"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":44,"order":277,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Earlier practice keeps pulling you forward, even against resistance.","snippet":"Even against his will, he is drawn onward by that earlier practice. Even the seeker of yoga goes beyond the sound of ritual words.","tags":["dhyana","abhyasa","yogabhrashta","shabdabrahma","samskara"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":45,"order":278,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Persistent striving eventually ripens into the highest fulfillment.","snippet":"But the yogi who keeps striving with effort, whose impurities have been cleared, and who has been perfected through many births, reaches …","tags":["dhyana-yoga","abhyasa","purification","many-births","param-gati"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":46,"order":279,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Inner mastery outranks every outer path.","snippet":"The yogi is greater than ascetics, greater than scholars, and greater than workers. Therefore, Arjuna, become a yogi.","tags":["dhyana-yoga","yogi","tapas","jnana","karma"]},{"chapter":6,"verse":47,"order":280,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Trusting devotion is the highest integration of yoga.","snippet":"Among all yogis, the one who worships me with trust, with the inner self absorbed in me, is considered the most fully united.","tags":["bhakti","shraddha","madgata","yukti","chapter-6"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":1,"order":281,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Refuge and practice open the way to complete knowing.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: Arjuna, fix your mind on Me, take refuge in Me, and practice yoga. Hear how you will know Me fully, without doubt.","tags":["madashraya","yoga","shraddha","chapter-7","jnana-vijnana"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":2,"order":282,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real knowing leaves no unfinished hunger for more.","snippet":"I will reveal to you knowledge together with direct realization in full. Knowing that, nothing more remains to be known here.","tags":["jnana","vijnana","complete_knowledge","chapter7","krishna_teaching"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":3,"order":283,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True knowing is rarer than striving, even among the successful.","snippet":"Among thousands of people, one may strive for perfection; among those striving, one may know Me in truth.","tags":["jnana-vijnana","tattvatah","rare-realisation","shraddha","krishna-knowledge"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":4,"order":284,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What changes is not the whole of what you are.","snippet":"Earth, water, fire, air, ether, mind, intellect, and ego: this is My eightfold lower nature.","tags":["prakriti","ahamkara","buddhi","manas","pancha-mahabhuta"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":5,"order":285,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What sustains the world is subtler than what the senses first show.","snippet":"Know My higher nature, which is different from this lower nature, O mighty-armed one. By that living nature, this world is sustained.","tags":["prakriti","para-prakriti","apara-prakriti","jiva-bhuta","sustaining-force"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":6,"order":286,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything that appears rises from one source and returns there.","snippet":"Know that all beings are born from these two natures. I am the source and the dissolution of the entire universe.","tags":["prakriti","srishti","pralaya","bhagavan","cosmic-source"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":7,"order":287,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything is held in one sustaining reality.","snippet":"O Dhananjaya, nothing exists higher than Me. All this world is strung on Me like pearls on a thread.","tags":["parama-prakriti","vibhuti","cosmic unity","krishna as support","thread and beads"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":8,"order":288,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The sacred is already inside ordinary experience.","snippet":"O son of Kunti, I am the taste in water, the light in the moon and sun, the syllable Om in all the Vedas, the sound in space, and the val…","tags":["vibhuti","om","manifestation","krishna-in-all-things","vedic-sound"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":9,"order":289,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The sacred is already inside nature, vitality, and discipline.","snippet":"I am the pure fragrance in the earth, the radiance in fire, the life in all beings, and the austerity in ascetics.","tags":["vibhuti","prakriti","tejas","tapas","bhagavan-immanence"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":10,"order":290,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All brilliance is borrowed from the same source.","snippet":"Know Me, O Partha, as the eternal seed of all beings. I am the intelligence of the intelligent and the brilliance of the brilliant.","tags":["vibhuti","source-of-intelligence","cosmic-immanence","seed-of-being","krishna-presence"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":11,"order":291,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Strength becomes clean when desire no longer fights dharma.","snippet":"Among the strong, I am strength free from desire and attachment. In beings, I am desire that does not oppose dharma, O best of the Bharatas.","tags":["kamaraga","dharmaaviruddha","indriya-shakti","bhagavan-vibhuti","desire-and-restraint"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":12,"order":292,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All qualities arise in the divine, yet the divine is not bound by any of them.","snippet":"Know that all states of being—sattvic, rajasic, and tamasic—arise from Me. I am not in them; they are in Me.","tags":["gunas","sattva-rajas-tamas","maya","krishna-immanence","transcendence"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":13,"order":293,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Three qualities can hide the imperishable reality from plain sight.","snippet":"Deluded by these three qualities, the whole world does not know me, who am beyond them and imperishable.","tags":["triguna","maya","avyaya","jnana-vijnana","perception"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":14,"order":294,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The way beyond the veil is not force, but refuge.","snippet":"My divine illusion, made of the three qualities, is hard to cross. Only those who take refuge in Me go beyond it.","tags":["maya","triguna","prapatti","sharanagati","bhakti"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":15,"order":295,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A corrupted mind cannot recognise what would free it.","snippet":"The deluded, the lowest among people, the wrongdoers, and those whose understanding has been stolen by the veil do not turn to me. They t…","tags":["maya","asuric-bhava","prapatti","delusion","krishna-refuge"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":16,"order":296,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Different needs can still lead to one real turning toward the divine.","snippet":"Four kinds of virtuous people worship Me, Arjuna: the distressed, the seeker of knowledge, the seeker of wealth, and the wise one, O best…","tags":["chaturvidha-bhaktah","artharthi","jijnasu","arta","jnani"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":17,"order":297,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Deep knowing and devoted love become a mutual bond.","snippet":"Among those four, the wise devotee who is ever united and one-pointed is श्रेष्ठ. For I am exceedingly dear to the wise one, and the wise…","tags":["bhakti","jnana","ananyabhakti","nityayukta","priyata"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":18,"order":298,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Deep knowing turns devotion into identity.","snippet":"All these are noble indeed, but the wise devotee is My very self. Established in yoga, that person is steadfast in Me as the unsurpassed …","tags":["bhakti","jnani-bhakta","ananya-bhakti","yuktatma","parama-gati"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":19,"order":299,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Deep seeing ends in surrender to the one reality in all things.","snippet":"After many births, the wise one surrenders to Me, knowing that Vasudeva is everything. Such a great soul is very rare.","tags":["vasudeva","prapatti","mahात्मa","sarvam iti","jnana-bhakti"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":20,"order":300,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire clouds judgment and sends the mind toward smaller refuges.","snippet":"Driven by desire, people whose understanding has been taken away turn to other radiant beings. They follow the rules of each, shaped by t…","tags":["kama","hrita-jnana","deva-upasana","prakriti","moham"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":21,"order":301,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Faith becomes firm where the devotee turns.","snippet":"Whatever form a devotee wants to worship with faith, I make that faith firm in that very form.","tags":["shraddha","devata-upasana","bhakti","faith","chapter-7"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":22,"order":302,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Faith draws the result, but the deeper order grants it.","snippet":"Endowed with that faith, that person seeks that worship, and receives those desires, granted by Me alone.","tags":["shraddha","devata-upasana","kamya-phala","bhagavata-order","chapter-7"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":23,"order":303,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Finite worship brings finite results; devotion returns you to Krishna.","snippet":"But the reward gained by those of limited understanding is finite. Those who worship the radiant beings go to the radiant beings; my devo…","tags":["shraddha","devata-upasana","bhakti","limited-fruit","krishna-gati"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":24,"order":304,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Form can hide the imperishable reality beneath it.","snippet":"The unwise think I have taken a visible form from the unseen. They do not know my imperishable, supreme nature.","tags":["avyakta","avatar","imperishable","supreme-nature","mohha"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":25,"order":305,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The hidden divine is missed by confused seeing, not by absence.","snippet":"Veiled by yoga-maya, I am not visible to everyone. Deluded people do not recognize me as unborn and imperishable.","tags":["yogamaya","ajam","avyayam","delusion","krishna-identity"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":26,"order":306,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything is visible to the divine; the divine remains unseen to ordinary minds.","snippet":"Arjuna, I know all beings of the past, the present, and the future. No one knows me.","tags":["omniscience","maya","aparoksha","jnana-vijnana","krishna-knowledge"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":27,"order":307,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire and aversion turn clear seeing into confusion.","snippet":"O descendant of Bharata, all beings fall into delusion at birth, from the confusion born of desire and aversion, O scorcher of foes.","tags":["dvandva","raga-dvesha","moha","samsara","attraction-aversion"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":28,"order":308,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear hearts stop wavering and move toward the divine with resolve.","snippet":"But those whose wrongdoing has been cleared away, and whose good deeds have matured, are freed from confusion and worship me with firm re…","tags":["dvandvamoha","punyakarma","dṛḍhavrata","bhajana","moral-purification"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":29,"order":309,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Refuge in the divine opens total understanding of reality, inner life, and action.","snippet":"Those who, seeking release from old age and death, take refuge in me, come to know Brahman, the whole field of the inner life, and all ac…","tags":["moksha","brahman","adhyatma","karma","refuge"]},{"chapter":7,"verse":30,"order":310,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Complete understanding remains steady even at the moment of departure.","snippet":"Those who know me together with the physical realm, the radiant powers, and the inner sacrifice know me even at the time of death.","tags":["adhibhuta","adhidaiva","adhiyajna","antakala","yuktacetas"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":1,"order":311,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clear seeing starts by asking what each word truly means.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Supreme Person, what is Brahman? What is the self? What is action? What is called the field of changing things, and what i…","tags":["akshara-brahma","arjuna-question","brahman","adhyatma","adhidaiva"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":2,"order":312,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Real understanding begins by asking what remains when life is ending.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Madhusudana, who is the sacrifice here, and how does he dwell in this body? And at the time of death, how are you known by…","tags":["adhiyajna","akshara-brahma","prayanakala","arjuna-question","disciplined-mind"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":3,"order":313,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What lasts, what you are, and what you do are not the same.","snippet":"The imperishable is the supreme reality. One\'s own nature is called the inner self. The offering that brings beings into existence is cal…","tags":["akshara","brahman","svabhava","adhyatma","visarga"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":4,"order":314,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The changing world, the cosmic order, and the inner witness are not separate.","snippet":"The perishable world is the lower realm; the cosmic person is the radiant being. I am the inner witness of sacrifice in this body, Arjuna.","tags":["adhibhuta","adhidaivata","adhiyajna","akshara-brahma","imperishable"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":5,"order":315,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The last remembered presence shapes the next state of being.","snippet":"Whoever remembers Me at the end and leaves the body attains My state; there is no doubt.","tags":["antakala","smarana","madbhava","mrityu","bhakti"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":6,"order":316,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The end follows the state you have trained.","snippet":"Whatever state a person remembers at the end, that state is reached, because the mind has been shaped by it.","tags":["antakala","smarana","bhava","manas","samskara"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":7,"order":317,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action and remembrance can happen together without conflict.","snippet":"Therefore, remember Me at all times and fight. With mind and intellect offered to Me, you will surely come to Me.","tags":["smarana","nishkama-karma","mind-offering","battlefield-dharma","bhakti-yoga"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":8,"order":318,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What the mind has practiced most will claim you at the end.","snippet":"One who departs while remembering the divine person with a mind trained by practice and fixed on nothing else reaches that supreme divine…","tags":["abhyasa","antakala","manas","parama-purusha","smarana"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":9,"order":319,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Hold the ungraspable source in mind, not the passing form.","snippet":"Whoever remembers the wise, ancient, ruler, subtler than the subtle, supporter of all, beyond thought, radiant like the sun, and beyond d…","tags":["akshara-brahma","smarana","anuchintana","tamas","adhyatma"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":10,"order":320,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady devotion carries awareness beyond the body\'s final threshold.","snippet":"At the time of departure, one who leaves the body with an unmoving mind, devotion, and the power of yoga, placing the life-force between …","tags":["antakala","prana","bhrumadhya","yogabala","achala-manas"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":11,"order":321,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The imperishable is reached by giving up desire, not by feeding it.","snippet":"I will briefly tell you that imperishable state, which the knowers of the Vedas call imperishable, which the detached ascetics enter, and…","tags":["akshara","brahmacharya","vairagya","asceticism","moksha"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":12,"order":322,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Mastery of the senses and mind prepares one for the final passage.","snippet":"Closing all the doors of the senses, holding the mind in the heart, and placing the life-force in the head, one remains fixed in yoga-dis…","tags":["pratyahara","prana","yogadharana","sense-withdrawal","death-practice"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":13,"order":323,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Final remembrance can carry consciousness beyond the body.","snippet":"Uttering Om, the one-syllable Brahman, and remembering Me, one who departs while leaving the body attains the supreme state.","tags":["om","akshara-brahma","antakale","smarana","parama-gati"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":14,"order":324,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Constant remembrance makes the divine easy to reach.","snippet":"Arjuna, for the one whose mind is wholly on me and who remembers me constantly, I am easy to reach.","tags":["ekachitta","smarana","nityayukta","bhakti","krishna-smarana"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":15,"order":325,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True arrival ends the need to come back.","snippet":"Great souls who reach me do not return to this painful, temporary cycle of birth.","tags":["moksha","punarjanma","mahात्मa","parama-siddhi","krishna"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":16,"order":326,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even the highest attainments return, but union with Krishna does not.","snippet":"All worlds up to Brahma\'s realm return again, Arjuna. But having reached me, O son of Kunti, there is no rebirth.","tags":["brahmaloka","punaravarti","rebirth","moksha","krishna"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":17,"order":327,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Cosmic time reveals how small ordinary urgency is.","snippet":"Those who know that Brahma’s day lasts a thousand yugas, and his night lasts a thousand yugas, know day and night truly.","tags":["brahma-day","cosmic-time","yuga-cycle","creation-dissolution","akshara-brahma"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":18,"order":328,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything formed returns to the unmanifest in time.","snippet":"At the start of Brahma\'s day, all beings arise from the unmanifest; at the start of Brahma\'s night, they dissolve back into that same unm…","tags":["avyakta","brahma-day","cosmic-cycle","pralaya","creation-dissolution"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":19,"order":329,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All formed things return and rise again under nature’s compulsion.","snippet":"O Arjuna, this entire group of beings is born again and again, and is dissolved at the coming of night; at the coming of day, it rises ag…","tags":["cosmic_cycle","pralaya","srishti","avyakta","prakriti"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":20,"order":330,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is deepest in reality cannot be destroyed by any ending.","snippet":"Beyond that unmanifest is another, eternal unmanifest. Even when all beings perish, it does not perish.","tags":["akshara","avyakta","sanatana","imperishable","cosmic dissolution"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":21,"order":331,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest arrival is beyond return.","snippet":"That is called the unmanifest and the imperishable. It is the highest goal. Having reached it, one does not return. It is my supreme abode.","tags":["akshara","avyakta","parama-gati","punaravritti","brahma-loka"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":22,"order":332,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Undivided devotion reaches the one presence that holds all beings.","snippet":"O Arjuna, the supreme person is reached through undivided devotion. All beings dwell within that being, and this entire world is pervaded…","tags":["ananyabhakti","parama-purusha","sarvabhuta","vyapti","bhakti-yoga"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":23,"order":333,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Not every departure leads the same way; some paths return you, others do not.","snippet":"I will tell you of the time when yogis do not return, and the time when they do, O best of the Bharatas.","tags":["akshara-brahma","return","nonreturn","departure","moksha"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":24,"order":334,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The final passage opens for those who know the supreme reality.","snippet":"Fire, daylight, the bright fortnight, and the six months of the northward course: those who depart then, knowing the supreme reality, go …","tags":["uttarayana","brahmavid","brahma","departure","akshara"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":25,"order":335,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Some routes only delay return; they do not end the cycle.","snippet":"In the path ruled by smoke, night, the dark fortnight, and the six months of the southern course, the yogi who departs there returns afte…","tags":["uttarayana","dakshinayana","lunar-path","post-death","return"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":26,"order":336,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Some choices free you from the cycle; others send you back into it.","snippet":"The bright and the dark are the two eternal paths of the world. One leads to non-return; the other brings return again.","tags":["uttarayana","dakshinayana","punaravritti","moksha","gati"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":27,"order":337,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Understanding the two paths keeps the mind unshaken.","snippet":"O Arjuna, the yogi who knows these two paths is never deluded. Therefore, remain steadfast in yoga at all times.","tags":["akshara-brahma","uttarayana","dakshinayana","moksha-marga","yoga-yukta"]},{"chapter":8,"verse":28,"order":338,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowing the way beyond rewards leads to the highest home.","snippet":"Knowing the two paths, the yogi goes beyond all the merits declared in the Vedas, sacrifices, austerities, and gifts, and reaches the pri…","tags":["akshara-brahma","moksha","punya","yajna","tapas"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":1,"order":339,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deepest truth frees only a heart that does not resist it.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: I will now tell you this most secret knowledge, joined with direct realization, to you who are not envious. Knowin…","tags":["raja-vidya","raja-guhya","anasuya","vijnana","moksha"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":2,"order":340,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest truth is both profound and simple to live.","snippet":"This is the king of all knowledge, the king of all secrets. It is supremely pure, directly knowable, aligned with dharma, easy to practic…","tags":["rajavidya","rajaguhya","pratyaksha","avyaya","dharma"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":3,"order":341,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Without trust, the highest teaching cannot carry you beyond repetition.","snippet":"O conqueror of foes, people without trust in this dharma do not reach Me and keep returning on the path of repeated death and rebirth.","tags":["shraddha","punarjanma","mrittyusamsara","raja-vidya","krishna"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":4,"order":342,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The supreme reality holds everything without being held by anything.","snippet":"All this universe is pervaded by my unmanifest form. All beings dwell in me, but I do not dwell in them.","tags":["avyakta","omnipresence","bhagavan","divine-immanence","cosmic-presence"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":5,"order":343,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The supreme reality sustains all beings without being contained by them.","snippet":"Behold My divine power: beings are not in Me, and yet I sustain all beings.","tags":["ishvara-yoga","omnipresence","bhutabhrit","bhutabhaavana","ch9"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":6,"order":344,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What moves everywhere still rests in the divine.","snippet":"As the great wind, moving everywhere, always rests in space, so all beings rest in Me.","tags":["omnipresence","vibhuti","bhagavan","cosmic-metaphor","shared-being"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":7,"order":345,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What seems like ending is only a return before another beginning.","snippet":"O son of Kunti, at the end of a cosmic cycle all beings enter my nature; at its beginning, I send them forth again.","tags":["prakriti","kalpa","cosmic_cycle","manifestation","omnipresence"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":8,"order":346,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Life unfolds through a power larger than individual will.","snippet":"Taking hold of my own nature, I repeatedly create this entire multitude of beings, helpless under the sway of nature.","tags":["prakriti","sarga","bhuta-grama","cosmic_cycle","divine_creation"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":9,"order":347,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action can continue without leaving a chain behind.","snippet":"Those actions of creation do not bind me, Dhananjaya, because I remain detached and indifferent to them.","tags":["prakriti","asakti","creation-cycle","detachment","cosmic-action"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":10,"order":348,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Change is not chaotic; it unfolds within a higher order.","snippet":"Nature, under my supervision, brings forth all moving and unmoving beings. Because of this, the world keeps changing, O son of Kunti.","tags":["prakriti","omnipresence","divine oversight","cosmic order","chapter 9"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":11,"order":349,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ordinary appearance can hide the highest reality.","snippet":"Fools despise Me when I dwell in a human form, not knowing My higher nature as the great Lord of all beings.","tags":["krishna-avatar","divine-form","misrecognition","human-appearance","bhagavan"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":12,"order":350,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A confused mind turns even hope, effort, and learning into waste.","snippet":"Those whose hopes, actions, and understanding are all wasted, confused minds take shelter in deluding, demonic, and shadowy nature.","tags":["moha","asuri-prakriti","rakshasi-prakriti","delusion","misdirected-action"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":13,"order":351,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True devotion begins when the mind recognises the imperishable source.","snippet":"But, Arjuna, the great-minded ones, relying on the divine nature, worship Me with one-pointed minds, knowing Me as the unborn and imperis…","tags":["daivi-prakriti","ananya-bhakti","bhajan","avyaya","bhagavan-source"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":14,"order":352,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady devotion becomes a life of continual remembrance.","snippet":"Ever united with Me, steadfast in vows, they worship Me by chanting, striving, and bowing with devotion.","tags":["bhakti","nityayukta","kirtana","namas","dhrdhabrata"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":15,"order":353,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The same reality can be approached as one, many, or all-encompassing.","snippet":"Others worship Me through the sacrifice of knowledge, seeing Me as one, as separate, or as the all-facing form.","tags":["jnana-yajna","vishvatomukha","ekatva","prthaktva","upasana"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":16,"order":354,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All sacred action is already filled with the divine presence.","snippet":"I am the sacrifice, I am the ritual, I am the offering, I am the herb, I am the mantra, I am the ghee, I am the fire, and I am the act of…","tags":["om","yajna","vedic-ritual","kratu","homa"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":17,"order":355,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All sources of life and meaning are gathered in Krishna.","snippet":"I am the father of this world, the mother, the supporter, and the grandfather. I am the object of knowledge, the purifier, the sacred syl…","tags":["om","vedas","cosmic-parent","vibhuti","source-of-world"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":18,"order":356,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything rests in one imperishable source.","snippet":"I am the goal, the supporter, the lord, the witness, the refuge, the friend, the source, the dissolution, the resting place, the treasure…","tags":["krishna-vibhuti","omnipresence","imperishable-seed","refuge","witness"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":19,"order":357,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Opposites do not stand outside the divine; they flow from it.","snippet":"I heat the world as the sun, I hold back the rain and send it forth. I am immortality and death, being and non-being, Arjuna.","tags":["vibhuti","divine omnipresence","rain","sun","amrita"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":20,"order":358,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Rewarded devotion still keeps you bound to return.","snippet":"Those who know the three Vedas, drink soma, and are purified by sacrifice pray for heaven. Having earned merit, they enjoy the divine ple…","tags":["soma","yajna","svarga","punya","trai-vidya"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":21,"order":359,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is won by wanting is lost by time.","snippet":"After enjoying the vast heaven-world, they return to the mortal world when their merit is exhausted. Thus, those who follow the ritual pa…","tags":["svarga","punya","tri-veda","punarjanma","kama"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":22,"order":360,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Unwavering devotion is met by unwavering support.","snippet":"Those who think of me alone and worship me with unwavering focus—I carry their welfare and security.","tags":["ananyabhakti","yogakshema","one-pointed-devotion","krishna-shelter","bhakti-assurance"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":23,"order":361,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All sincere worship reaches the one reality, even when the form is confused.","snippet":"Even those who, filled with trust, worship other radiant beings, worship Me alone, but in the wrong way, O son of Kunti.","tags":["other-deities","shraddha","exclusive-devotion","upasana","bhakti"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":24,"order":362,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every offering matters only when you know who receives it.","snippet":"For I am the enjoyer and lord of all sacrifices. But those people do not know me in truth, and so they fall away.","tags":["yajna","bhakti","ananya-bhakti","tattva-jnana","divine-receiver"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":25,"order":363,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devotion does not stay abstract; it carries you to its chosen end.","snippet":"Those devoted to the radiant beings reach the radiant beings. Those devoted to the ancestors reach the ancestors. Those devoted to spirit…","tags":["devata-upasana","bhakti","afterlife","worship","krishna"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":26,"order":364,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A small offering becomes complete when devotion fills it.","snippet":"Whoever offers me a leaf, a flower, a fruit, or water with devotion, I accept that devoted offering from the pure-hearted.","tags":["bhakti","naivedya","offering","prasad","sincerity"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":27,"order":365,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every action becomes complete when it is offered.","snippet":"Whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever you offer, whatever you give, and whatever austerity you practice, offer it to me.","tags":["madarpanam","offering","bhakti","daily action","austerity"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":28,"order":366,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when even the result is no longer yours to carry.","snippet":"In this way, you will be freed from the bonds of action and its results. Given over to renunciation-yoga, released, you will come to me.","tags":["karma-bandha","sannyasa-yoga","phala-tyaga","bhakti-offering","krishna-surrender"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":29,"order":367,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Equality is universal; intimacy is born through devotion.","snippet":"I am equal toward all beings. No one is hated by me, and no one is especially dear. But those who worship me with devotion dwell in me, a…","tags":["bhakti","samatva","mutual-indwelling","krishna-presence","devotional-intimacy"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":30,"order":368,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Undivided devotion can outweigh even a deeply flawed life.","snippet":"Even if a person of very bad conduct worships Me with undivided devotion, that person must be regarded as righteous, for the resolve is r…","tags":["ananyabhakti","sudurachara","bhakti-m","grace","moral-rehabilitation"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":31,"order":369,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devotion quickly changes a person and protects them from ruin.","snippet":"One who is devoted to Me quickly becomes righteous and attains lasting peace. O son of Kunti, declare it boldly: My devotee never perishes.","tags":["bhakti","sharanagati","lasting-peace","krishna-protection","fearlessness"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":32,"order":370,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"No birth or status can block one who takes refuge.","snippet":"O Partha, even those born in difficult circumstances, and women, merchants, and workers, can reach the highest state by taking refuge in me.","tags":["sharanagati","parama-gati","varna","stri","papa-yoni"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":33,"order":371,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What does not last cannot finally satisfy; turn your life toward the divine.","snippet":"If even pure Brahmins and royal sages devoted to the divine reach the highest state, what to speak of you? So, having come into this impe…","tags":["bhakti","anitya","asukha","rajarshi","worldweariness"]},{"chapter":9,"verse":34,"order":372,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Total orientation toward the divine becomes the way to reach the divine.","snippet":"Fix your mind on me. Be devoted to me. Worship me. Bow to me. United with me in this way, and fully oriented toward me, you will come to me.","tags":["bhakti","matparayana","namaskur","worship","surrender"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":1,"order":373,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Deeper truth arrives as care for the one who is ready.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: Listen again, O mighty-armed one, to my supreme word, which I will speak for your welfare because you are deeply d…","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-speech","supreme-word","listener-dear","chapter-10"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":2,"order":374,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even the highest knowers stand inside the source they seek.","snippet":"The hosts of devas do not know my origin, nor do the great sages, for I am the beginning of the devas and the great sages in every way.","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-origin","devas","maharshi","cosmic-source"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":3,"order":375,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear recognition of the divine ends confusion and frees action.","snippet":"One who knows Me as unborn, beginningless, and the great lord of all worlds is undeluded among mortals and is freed from every wrong deed.","tags":["krishna","lokamaheshvara","ajanma","anadi","delusion"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":4,"order":376,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All human qualities arise from the same source.","snippet":"Understanding, wisdom, freedom from confusion, forgiveness, truth, self-restraint, calmness, pleasure, pain, coming into being, ceasing t…","tags":["vibhuti","human qualities","fearlessness","self-restraint","bhagavan"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":5,"order":377,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All qualities are expressions of the same divine source.","snippet":"Nonviolence, equanimity, contentment, austerity, charity, honor, and dishonor—all these different states of beings arise from Me alone.","tags":["vibhuti","ahimsa","samata","tapas","daana"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":6,"order":378,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All lineages and worlds emerge from Krishna’s mind.","snippet":"The seven great sages, the four ancient sages, and the fourteen Manus were born from my mind. The people of these worlds descend from them.","tags":["vibhuti","manu","saptarishi","cosmic lineage","srsti"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":7,"order":379,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True recognition of Krishna\'s presence makes devotion unshakable.","snippet":"One who truly knows this glory and this yoga of mine becomes steadfast in yoga without doubt.","tags":["vibhuti","bhakti","yoga","krishna","unshakable-devotion"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":8,"order":380,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowing the source turns understanding into devotion.","snippet":"I am the source of all; everything moves from me. Knowing this, the wise worship me with wholehearted devotion.","tags":["vibhuti","omnipresence","bhakti","source-of-all","wholehearted-devotion"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":9,"order":381,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Shared remembrance keeps devotion alive.","snippet":"With minds fixed on Me and lives offered to Me, My devotees speak of Me to one another, and find continual joy in that shared devotion.","tags":["bhakti","remembrance","satsang","shared-devotion","krishna-katha"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":10,"order":382,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady devotion itself draws forth the understanding that reaches the divine.","snippet":"To those who are always devoted and worship Me with love, I give the discernment that leads them to Me.","tags":["bhakti","buddhi-yoga","steady-devotion","krishna-grace","discernment"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":11,"order":383,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Compassion becomes knowledge that burns away inner darkness.","snippet":"To show them compassion, I destroy the darkness born of ignorance with the shining lamp of knowledge, dwelling in their own being.","tags":["bhakti","jnana","anukampa","avidya","knowledge-lamp"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":12,"order":384,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Recognition turns into surrender when the highest reality stands revealed.","snippet":"Arjuna said: You are the supreme reality, the highest refuge, the purest one, the eternal divine person, the first being, unborn, and all…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","param-brahma","all-pervading","unborn"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":13,"order":385,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The deepest recognition is echoed by the wise and by Krishna himself.","snippet":"All the sages speak of you this way: the divine sage Narada, Asita, Devala, and Vyasa. You yourself also say this to me.","tags":["narada","vyasa","divine-manifestations","krishna-glory","bhakti-recognition"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":14,"order":386,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"True recognition begins where ordinary beings cannot see.","snippet":"I accept as true all that you have said, O Keshava. O Bhagavan, neither the devas nor the asuras know your manifested form.","tags":["vishvarupa","arjuna-prayer","bhagavan","devas","asuras"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":15,"order":387,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The supreme one is known fully only by the supreme one.","snippet":"O Supreme Person, you alone know yourself by yourself, O source of all beings, lord of all beings, divine of the divine, ruler of the world.","tags":["purushottama","vishvarupa","bhagavan","arjuna-stuti","cosmic-lord"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":16,"order":388,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Only the source can fully name its own presence in the world.","snippet":"Only you can fully describe your own divine manifestations, by which you pervade and sustain all these worlds.","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-manifestations","arjuna-prayer","cosmic-pervasion","bhagavan"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":17,"order":389,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Devotion needs a form the mind can return to again and again.","snippet":"O Yogi, how shall I know You by constant contemplation? In what forms should You be contemplated, O Blessed One?","tags":["vibhuti","arjuna-prayer","krishna-remembrance","bhagavan","contemplation"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":18,"order":390,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"True devotion never feels finished hearing the beloved.","snippet":"O Janardana, tell me again in detail of Your yogic power and Your manifestations, for I am not satisfied hearing Your nectar-like words.","tags":["vibhuti","janardana","arjuna","krishna-glories","bhakti"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":19,"order":391,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine can be named briefly, never exhausted.","snippet":"Krishna said: I will tell you briefly of my divine manifestations, chief of them, Arjuna, for there is no end to their विस्तार.","tags":["vibhuti","janardana","limitless-manifestations","divine-presence","krishna-teaching"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":20,"order":392,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything that exists is held within one enduring presence.","snippet":"I am the Self, O Gudakesha, seated in the heart of all beings. I am the beginning, the middle, and the end of all beings.","tags":["vibhuti","antaryamin","sarvabhuta","janardana","krishna"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":21,"order":393,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every radiance is a sign of one presence.","snippet":"Among the sons of Aditi, I am Vishnu; among radiant things, I am the sun with rays. I am the brilliance in the Maruts, and among stars, I…","tags":["vibhuti","cosmic manifestations","surya","chandra","adityas"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":22,"order":394,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine is not elsewhere; it is the awareness within everything.","snippet":"Among the Vedas, I am the Sama Veda; among the radiant beings, I am Indra. Among the senses, I am the mind; among living beings, I am con…","tags":["vibhuti","sama-veda","indra","manas","chetana"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":23,"order":395,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Greatness in the world is a visible sign of Krishna\'s presence.","snippet":"Among the Rudras, I am Shankara; among the Yakshas and Rakshasas, I am Kubera. Among the Vasus, I am fire, and among mountain peaks, I am…","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-manifestations","meru","kubera","rudras"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":24,"order":396,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Greatness in the world is a trace of Krishna everywhere.","snippet":"Among priests, know Me as Brihaspati; among commanders, I am Skanda; among waters, I am the ocean.","tags":["vibhuti","brihaspati","skanda","ocean","divine-manifestations"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":25,"order":397,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine appears through the noblest forms of speech, ritual, and nature.","snippet":"Among great sages I am Bhrigu; among words I am the one imperishable syllable. Among sacrifices I am the sacrifice of silent repetition; …","tags":["vibhuti","pranava","japa-yajna","himalaya","bhrigu"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":26,"order":398,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The finest forms in creation are windows into Krishna.","snippet":"Among all trees I am the sacred fig tree. Among divine sages I am Narada; among celestial musicians, Chitraratha; among perfected sages, …","tags":["vibhuti","narada","kapila","ashvattha","divine-manifestations"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":27,"order":399,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Greatness in the world is a visible trace of Krishna.","snippet":"Among horses, know me as Ucchaihshravas, born from nectar. Among royal elephants, I am Airavata, and among humans, I am the king.","tags":["vibhuti","ucchaihshravas","airavata","naradhipa","krishna-manifestation"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":28,"order":400,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Power, fertility, and danger all reveal the same source.","snippet":"Among weapons, I am the thunderbolt; among cows, I am the wish-fulfilling cow. I am the cause of procreation, and among serpents, I am Va…","tags":["vibhuti","kamadhuk","vasuki","kandarpa","manifestations"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":29,"order":401,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine is visible in every order of existence.","snippet":"Among serpents I am Ananta; among water beings I am Varuna. Among ancestors I am Aryaman; among those who govern, I am Yama.","tags":["vibhuti","ananta","varuna","aryaman","yama"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":30,"order":402,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Power, devotion, and majesty are all windows into one presence.","snippet":"Among the daityas I am Prahlada; among calculators I am Time. Among beasts I am the lion, and among birds I am Garuda.","tags":["vibhuti","prahlada","garuda","time","divine-manifestations"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":31,"order":403,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"One reality appears as every noble force.","snippet":"Among purifiers, I am the wind. Among wielders of weapons, I am Rama. Among aquatic beings, I am the crocodile. Among flowing rivers, I a…","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-glories","ganga","rama","natural-forces"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":32,"order":404,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All creation and all truth-seeking speech point back to Krishna.","snippet":"I am the beginning, the middle, and the end of all creation, Arjuna. Among all forms of knowledge, I am the knowledge of the true self; a…","tags":["vibhuti","adhyatmavidya","vadah","creation-cycle","truth-seeking"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":33,"order":405,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even letters and time carry Krishna\'s presence.","snippet":"Among letters I am the letter A. Among compounds I am the dual compound. I am endless time itself, and I am the all-facing sustainer.","tags":["vibhuti","akara","dvandva","akala","dhata"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":34,"order":406,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even death and virtue are expressions of the same divine source.","snippet":"I am death that takes everything, and the source of all future beings. Among women, I am fame, fortune, speech, memory, intelligence, ste…","tags":["vibhuti","death","birth","stri-guna","divine-manifestations"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":35,"order":407,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sacred sound, time, and spring all carry the same presence.","snippet":"Among hymns I am the Brihat-Sama; among meters I am Gayatri. Among months I am Margashirsha; among seasons I am spring.","tags":["vibhuti","gayatri","brihat-sama","margashirsha","spring"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":36,"order":408,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What shines through victory and resolve is not separate from the divine.","snippet":"Among deceivers I am gambling, among the vigorous I am splendor. I am victory, I am resolve, and I am the goodness of the good.","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-manifestation","resolve","victory","sattva"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":37,"order":409,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Greatness in many forms is one presence showing itself.","snippet":"Among the Vrishnis I am Vasudeva; among the Pandavas I am Dhananjaya. Among sages I am Vyasa, and among poets I am Ushana, the poet.","tags":["vibhuti","krishna-glories","vasudeva","dhananjaya","vyasa"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":38,"order":410,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True power is measured by restraint, silence, and clear understanding.","snippet":"Among enforcers, I am punishment; among those seeking victory, I am policy. Among secrets, I am silence; among the wise, I am knowledge.","tags":["vibhuti","niti","mauna","danda","jnana"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":39,"order":411,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All existence grows from one hidden source.","snippet":"Arjuna, I am the seed of all beings. Without me, nothing moving or unmoving could exist.","tags":["vibhuti","sarvabhuta","beej","krishna-omnipresence","moving-unmoving"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":40,"order":412,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"No list can contain the divine\'s endless expressions.","snippet":"O scorcher of foes, my divine manifestations have no end. What I have described to you is only a brief summary of my vast manifestations.","tags":["vibhuti","limitless manifestations","divine presence","cosmic expanse","krishna teaching"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":41,"order":413,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every genuine greatness is only a spark of my radiance.","snippet":"Whatever being or thing is endowed with splendour, beauty, or power—know that to have arisen from a spark of my radiance.","tags":["vibhuti","tejas","glory","manifestation","divine-radiance"]},{"chapter":10,"verse":42,"order":414,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The whole universe rests in a single fragment of the divine.","snippet":"Or, Arjuna, what is the need for all this detailed knowledge? I sustain this entire universe with a single fragment of myself.","tags":["vibhuti","krishna","cosmic-form","omnipresence","manifestation"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":1,"order":415,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clarity arrives when the hidden teaching is finally heard as personal grace.","snippet":"Arjuna said: By the gracious words you spoke for my benefit alone, my delusion has been dispelled.","tags":["arjuna","moha","parama-guhya","adhyatma","krishna-grace"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":2,"order":416,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"All change is clear only beside what does not change.","snippet":"O lotus-eyed one, I have heard from You in detail about the arising and passing away of all beings, and also about Your imperishable maje…","tags":["vishwarupa","imperishable","mahatmya","arjuna-prayer","krishna-glory"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":3,"order":417,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Belief becomes complete only when it wants to see.","snippet":"O Supreme Person, everything you have said about yourself is true. Yet I wish to see your divine form.","tags":["vishwarupa","darshana","arjuna","parameshvara","ishvara-rupa"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":4,"order":418,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Real vision begins when control gives way to asking.","snippet":"If you think I can see that form, Lord, then show me your imperishable self, Master of yoga.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","sharanagati","divya-rupa","yogeshvara"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":5,"order":419,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine cannot be contained in one shape.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: See, Partha, my forms in hundreds and thousands, diverse, divine, and of many colors and shapes.","tags":["vishwarupa","divine-forms","cosmic-vision","krishna-revelation","many-shapes"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":6,"order":420,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The familiar universe is only a small part of what Krishna reveals.","snippet":"See the twelve Adityas, the eight Vasus, the eleven Rudras, the two Ashvins, and the forty-nine Maruts. See many wonders never seen befor…","tags":["vishvarupa","adityas","rudras","ashvins","maruts"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":7,"order":421,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Everything you seek is already gathered in the divine form.","snippet":"Behold the entire universe, with all that moves and does not move, gathered here in one place in My body. See whatever else you wish to s…","tags":["vishwarupa","cosmic form","all-pervading","divine vision","arjuna"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":8,"order":422,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ordinary sight cannot hold the infinite; grace must widen the eye.","snippet":"You cannot see me with these ordinary eyes. I give you divine sight, so you may behold my supreme power.","tags":["vishwarupa","divya-chakshus","ishvara-shakti","darshana","krishna-cosmic-form"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":9,"order":423,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The answer is not a theory; it arrives as a vision.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Having spoken thus, O King, the great lord of yoga, Hari, revealed to Arjuna the supreme divine form.","tags":["vishwarupa","mahayogeshvara","hari","divine-form","arjuna-vision"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":10,"order":424,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The divine form cannot be held inside one human image.","snippet":"With many mouths and eyes, with countless wondrous forms, adorned with many divine ornaments and many uplifted divine weapons.","tags":["vishwarupa","cosmic-form","divine-vision","multiform","sanjaya"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":11,"order":425,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The divine presence is beautiful, boundless, and impossible to face from only one side.","snippet":"Wearing divine garlands and garments, anointed with divine fragrances, wondrous in every way, endless, and facing everywhere.","tags":["vishvarupa","anantam","visvatomukham","divya-malya","divya-ambara"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":12,"order":426,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Even the brightest familiar light cannot measure the cosmic form\'s radiance.","snippet":"If a thousand suns rose together in the sky, their light would still barely match that great being\'s radiance.","tags":["vishwarupa","cosmic-form","divine-radiance","arjuna-awe","suryasahasra"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":13,"order":427,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"One form can contain the whole universe.","snippet":"There Arjuna saw the entire universe gathered in one place, divided in countless ways within the body of the Lord of the gods.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","universal-vision","krishna-glory"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":14,"order":428,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"A glimpse of the vast can turn shock into surrender.","snippet":"Then, overwhelmed with wonder, Arjuna’s hair stood on end. He bowed his head to the divine and spoke with folded hands.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","awe","folded-hands","pranama"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":15,"order":429,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The many forms of existence appear within one vast body.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O divine one, I see all the gods in your body, and all kinds of distinct beings, Brahma seated on the lotus, Shiva, all the …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic_form","brahma","sages"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":16,"order":430,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The largest reality has no edge the mind can grasp.","snippet":"I see You with many arms, bellies, mouths, and eyes, everywhere without end. I see no beginning, middle, or end of You, O Lord of all, O …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","limitless-form","awe","cosmic-vision"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":17,"order":431,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"What is most real cannot be fully held by sight.","snippet":"I see you wearing a crown, holding a mace and discus, blazing everywhere, hard to behold, and immeasurable — like fire and the sun in bri…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","cosmic-form","immeasurable","awe"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":18,"order":432,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"What appears overwhelming is actually the world’s deepest support.","snippet":"You are the imperishable supreme reality, the highest support of this world, the guardian of eternal dharma, and the eternal person.","tags":["vishwarupa","akshara","sanatana-dharma","purusha","krishna"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":19,"order":433,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"What overwhelms the mind can also dissolve its resistance.","snippet":"I see you as beginningless, middleless, and endless; of infinite power, with infinite arms, with eyes like the moon and the sun, with mou…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","infinite-arms","surrender"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":20,"order":434,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"One vision can overwhelm every boundary you thought was real.","snippet":"The space between heaven and earth and all directions are filled by You alone. Seeing Your wondrous and fierce form, the three worlds tre…","tags":["vishvarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","awe","surrender"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":21,"order":435,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Even the highest beings bow when the vast form appears.","snippet":"The hosts of the radiant beings enter into you. Some, frightened, join their palms and sing your names and qualities. Great seers and per…","tags":["vishvarupa","arjuna","surasangha","maharshi","siddha"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":22,"order":436,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Even the highest beings stand astonished before Krishna\'s vastness.","snippet":"The eleven Rudras, the twelve Adityas, the eight Vasus, the twelve Sadhyas, the Visvedevas, the two Ashvins, the forty-nine Maruts, the a…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","celestial-beings","awe"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":23,"order":437,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"A vision of total vastness can shake every observer at once.","snippet":"O mighty-armed one, seeing your great form with many mouths and eyes, many arms, thighs, and feet, many bellies, and terrible fangs, all …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","awe","overwhelm"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":24,"order":438,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"A true vision can shatter the mind before it can steady it.","snippet":"O Vishnu, seeing you touching the sky, blazing with many colors, with mouths spread wide and bright, vast eyes, my inner being is shaken.…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","awe","fear","krishna"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":25,"order":439,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"True awe ends control and turns the heart toward surrender.","snippet":"Seeing your flaming, terrible mouths with their fangs, I can no longer find directions or peace. Be gracious, Lord of the divine beings, …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","surrender","awe","cosmic-form"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":26,"order":440,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Even the greatest warriors are swallowed by what exceeds them.","snippet":"Bhishma, Drona, Karna, and all the sons of Dhritarashtra, along with the hosts of kings and our own chief warriors, are rushing into your…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","kurukshetra","mahabharata","bhishma"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":27,"order":441,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"All fighters are already being consumed by time.","snippet":"Your blazing, terrible mouths swallow them in haste. Some are seen caught between your teeth, with crushed heads.","tags":["vishwarupa","time","cosmic-form","kurukshetra","arjuna-vision"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":28,"order":442,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"All motion is already rushing toward its end.","snippet":"As many streams of water rush naturally toward the sea, so these great warriors of the world enter your blazing mouths.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","inevitability","river-metaphor"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":29,"order":443,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Blind desire runs straight into its own ruin.","snippet":"As moths rush with great speed into a blazing fire to their destruction, so these people rush with great speed into your mouths to their …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","moths","destruction"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":30,"order":444,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Total power leaves no room for control.","snippet":"You lick up all the worlds from every side with your blazing mouths. Your fierce radiance fills the whole universe and burns it, O Vishnu.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","world-devouring","awe"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":31,"order":445,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Fear bows first, then asks to know what stands before it.","snippet":"Tell me who You are in this fierce form. Salutations to You, best of the radiant beings; be gracious. I wish to know You, the primal one,…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","surrender","prayer","cosmic-form"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":32,"order":446,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is ending was never in your hands to preserve.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: I am Time, the great destroyer of worlds, here to end all beings. Even without you, the warriors standing in the o…","tags":["vishwarupa","kala","cosmic-time","arjuna","kurukshetra"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":33,"order":447,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Act fully, but let the larger order carry the result.","snippet":"Therefore, rise and win fame. Conquer your enemies and enjoy a prosperous kingdom. They have already been slain by me; become only the in…","tags":["nimitta","sharanagati","kurukshetra","vishwarupa","karma-yoga"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":34,"order":448,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The battle is already decided; your task is only to act.","snippet":"Drona, Bhishma, Jayadratha, Karna, and the other great warriors have already been slain by Me. Do not falter; fight, and you will surely …","tags":["kurukshetra","vishwarupa","arjuna","fearlessness","battle-command"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":35,"order":449,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Awe can break speech before it becomes prayer.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Hearing Krishna\'s words, Arjuna trembled, folded his hands, bowed again and again, and spoke to Krishna in a choked voice, …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","sanjaya","awe","prostration"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":36,"order":450,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The divine name can turn fear into devotion and disorder into reverence.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Hrishikesha, by chanting Your names and glories, the whole world rejoices and becomes devoted. By that chanting, frightene…","tags":["vishwarupa","hrishikesha","stuti","nama-kirtana","arjuna-prayer"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":37,"order":451,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"What exceeds all categories naturally draws surrender.","snippet":"O great one, why would the perfected beings not bow to you, the greatest teacher, the first maker even of Brahma? Endless Lord of radiant…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","cosmic-form","brahma","surrender"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":38,"order":452,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The one you seek is the ground that already holds everything.","snippet":"You are the first divine presence, the ancient person, the supreme refuge of this universe. You are the knower, the knowable, and the hig…","tags":["vishwarupa","anantarupa","jagannivasa","purusha","parama-dhama"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":39,"order":453,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"All powers and forces bow inside the one you face.","snippet":"You are air, Yama, fire, Varuna, the moon, Prajapati, and the great ancestor. I bow to you a thousand times, and again and again.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","cosmic-form","namas","prajapati"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":40,"order":454,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Total awe ends the illusion of separation.","snippet":"Salutations to you from the front, from behind, and from every side. You are endless power and immeasurable might; you pervade all and th…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","surrender","cosmic-form","omnipresence"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":41,"order":455,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Familiarity without recognition becomes disrespect; awe restores the right relation.","snippet":"Thinking of you as a friend, I addressed you carelessly: “O Krishna, O Yadava, O friend.” Not knowing your greatness, I spoke in negligen…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","forgiveness","awe","bhakti"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":42,"order":456,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Familiarity can hide greatness until awe breaks through.","snippet":"Whatever disrespect I showed you in jest, while walking, resting, sitting, eating, alone or before others, I ask your immeasurable forgiv…","tags":["arjuna-prayer","forgiveness","vishwarupa","reverence","humility"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":43,"order":457,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Recognition of the highest power dissolves all comparison.","snippet":"You are the father of all moving and unmoving beings, the highest object of reverence, and the greatest teacher. In the three worlds, no …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","reverence","guru","unmatched-power"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":44,"order":458,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"True reverence asks forgiveness without excuses.","snippet":"Therefore, bowing down my body, I seek to please You, the worthy Lord of praise. Like a father bearing a son’s fault, a friend bearing a …","tags":["arjuna-prayer","forgiveness","vishwarupa","humility","bhakti"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":45,"order":459,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"A vision can awaken joy and fear at once.","snippet":"I have never seen this form before. Seeing it, I am filled with joy, yet my mind is troubled by fear. Show me again your gentle divine fo…","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna-prayer","devotional-awe","four-armed-form","surrender"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":46,"order":460,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"The infinite can overwhelm; devotion asks for a form the heart can bear.","snippet":"I want to see you again in your crowned form, with mace and discus in your hands. O Thousand-Armed One, O Universal Form, return to that …","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","chaturbhuja","krishna","bhakti"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":47,"order":461,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is most sacred is seen only by grace.","snippet":"Krishna said: O Arjuna, I have shown you this supreme, radiant, endless, original form through my grace. No one except you has seen it be…","tags":["vishwarupa","grace","divine-revelation","arjuna","cosmic-form"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":48,"order":462,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest vision cannot be forced; it arrives only through grace.","snippet":"I cannot be seen in this form in the human world by study of the Vedas, sacrifice, charity, severe austerity, or ritual acts—except by yo…","tags":["vishvarupa","krishna-grace","bhagavad-darshana","austerity","ritual-limits"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":49,"order":463,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Fear must drop before the deeper vision can be seen.","snippet":"Do not be distressed or confused by this fierce form of mine. Free from fear and calm-minded, look again upon this very form of mine.","tags":["vishwarupa","abhaya","arjuna","cosmic-form","bhaya"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":50,"order":464,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"A vision can shake you; compassion brings you back.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: After speaking thus to Arjuna, Vasudeva revealed his own form again. The great one then reassured the frightened Arjuna, ta…","tags":["vishwarupa","sanjaya","gentle-form","reassurance","arjuna-fear"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":51,"order":465,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Gentleness restores the mind after overwhelming awe.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Seeing your gentle human form, Janardana, I am calm again and restored to my natural state.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","janardana","restoration","gentle-form"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":52,"order":466,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The vision Arjuna saw is beyond ordinary access, even for radiant beings.","snippet":"Krishna said: The form you have seen is very hard to behold. Even the radiant beings long forever to see it.","tags":["vishwarupa","arjuna","cosmic-form","darshan","bhakti"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":53,"order":467,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deepest vision comes through devotion, not mere accomplishment.","snippet":"I cannot be seen in this form through the Vedas, austerity, charity, or sacrifice, as you have seen me.","tags":["vishvarupa","ananya-bhakti","darshana","upasana","tapas"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":54,"order":468,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Undivided devotion reaches what effort cannot.","snippet":"But only through undivided devotion can I be truly known, seen, and entered, Arjuna.","tags":["ananyabhakti","vishwarupa","entry","direct-realisation","surrender"]},{"chapter":11,"verse":55,"order":469,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devotion matures into freedom when attachment and hostility are gone.","snippet":"O Pandava, the devotee who works for Me alone, takes Me as the highest goal, is devoted to Me, is free from attachment, and bears no enmi…","tags":["bhakti","ananyabhakti","sangavर्जita","nirvaira","matparah"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":1,"order":470,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Devotion can face the divine as form or as formless reality.","snippet":"Arjuna said: Those devotees who worship You with constant devotion, and those who worship the imperishable, unmanifest reality—who among …","tags":["bhakti","akshara","avyakta","upasana","yogavittama"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":2,"order":471,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Full trust and steady remembrance make devotion complete.","snippet":"Those who focus their mind on me, worship me with unwavering devotion, and are filled with supreme trust are, in my view, the highest yogis.","tags":["bhakti","shraddha","nityayukta","upasana","manas"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":3,"order":472,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deepest devotion reaches what never changes.","snippet":"Those who worship the unchanging, the indefinable, the unmanifest, the all-pervading, the unthinkable, the unmoving, the eternal, the imp…","tags":["bhakti","akshara","avyakta","sarvatraga","indriya-samyama"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":4,"order":473,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Reach the divine by mastering yourself and caring for everyone.","snippet":"Those who restrain the senses, remain even-minded everywhere, and delight in the welfare of all beings reach me alone.","tags":["indriya-nigraha","samatva","sarvabhuta-hita","bhakti","equal-vision"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":5,"order":474,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The subtlest path is hardest for a body-bound mind.","snippet":"For those whose minds cling to the unmanifest, the struggle is greater. The unmanifest path is hard to reach for embodied beings.","tags":["avyakta","bhakti","indriya-nigraha","embodied-mindedness","spiritual-practice"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":6,"order":475,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Total devotion turns every action into worship.","snippet":"But those who surrender all actions to Me, take Me as their highest aim, and worship Me with single-pointed devotion, meditating on Me al…","tags":["bhakti","ananya-bhakti","karma-sannyasa","upasana","single-pointed-devotion"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":7,"order":476,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A mind fixed on Krishna is met by Krishna\'s saving presence.","snippet":"I quickly become the one who lifts those whose minds are fixed on me from the ocean of mortal existence, O Partha.","tags":["bhakti","surrender","mortal-existence","krishna-protection","manas"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":8,"order":477,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A divided mind settles when both thought and feeling rest in the divine.","snippet":"Fix your mind on me alone. Place your discerning mind in me, and you will live in me beyond doubt.","tags":["bhakti","manas","buddhi","ekagrata","surrender"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":9,"order":478,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Practice can lead the mind where stillness cannot yet go.","snippet":"If you cannot steadily fix your mind on me, then, Dhananjaya, seek me through practice yoga.","tags":["bhakti-yoga","abhyasa","manas","shraddha","practice"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":10,"order":479,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Offered action can succeed where practice still fails.","snippet":"If you are unable even to practice, then be devoted to working for Me. By doing actions for My sake, you will attain perfection.","tags":["bhakti-yoga","matkarmaparah","seva","practice","offering"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":11,"order":480,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Let go of the result; the action itself is the practice.","snippet":"If you still cannot do even this while taking refuge in my yoga, then, self-controlled, renounce all fruits of action.","tags":["bhakti-yoga","karmaphala-tyaga","yatayatmana","vairagya","surrender"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":12,"order":481,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Peace begins when you stop clinging to what your action produces.","snippet":"Knowledge is better than practice; meditation is better than knowledge. Renouncing the fruits of action is better than meditation, and pe…","tags":["karmaphalatyaga","dhyana","tyaga","shanti","bhakti-yoga"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":13,"order":482,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devotion shows up as friendliness, forgiveness, and emotional steadiness.","snippet":"One who hates no being, is friendly and compassionate, free from possessiveness and ego, equal in pleasure and pain, and forgiving.","tags":["bhakti","karuna","ahankara","mamatva","kshama"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":14,"order":483,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real devotion is a steady mind already placed beyond itself.","snippet":"The devoted yogi is always content, self-controlled, and steady in resolve. One whose mind and discerning mind are offered to Me is dear …","tags":["bhakti","manas","buddhi","santosha","yoga"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":15,"order":484,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True devotion leaves no wake of disturbance.","snippet":"The one who disturbs no one and is disturbed by no one, and who is free from delight, envy, fear, and agitation, is dear to me.","tags":["bhakti","equanimity","fearlessness","non-reactivity","krishna-priya"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":16,"order":485,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True closeness releases craving, anxiety, and compulsive beginning.","snippet":"One who has no expectation, is pure, skilled, detached, free from anxiety, and has given up all undertakings is dear to me, my devotee.","tags":["bhakti","anapeksha","udasinata","surrender","sattva"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":17,"order":486,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devotion becomes steady when liking and disliking no longer rule the heart.","snippet":"One who neither rejoices, hates, grieves, nor craves, and who has given up attachment to both good and bad actions, is dear to me.","tags":["bhakti","vairagya","attachment","aversion","equanimity"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":18,"order":487,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real devotion stays even when life feels hostile or kind.","snippet":"One who is equal to enemy and friend, honor and dishonor, heat and cold, pleasure and pain, and is free from attachment is dear to Me.","tags":["bhakti","equanimity","honor-disgrace","attachment","samatva"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":19,"order":488,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Praise and blame lose power over the one who stands steady.","snippet":"Equal in praise and blame, silent, content with whatever comes, homeless, steady-minded—the devoted person is dear to me.","tags":["bhakti","sthitaprajna","nindastuti","aniketa","santosha"]},{"chapter":12,"verse":20,"order":489,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Faithful practice turns devotion into closeness.","snippet":"Those devotees who trust, take refuge in Me, and faithfully live this nectar-like teaching are exceedingly dear to Me.","tags":["bhakti","shraddha","matparah","devotee","priya"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":1,"order":490,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Real knowing starts by separating the seen from the seer.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Keshava, I wish to understand nature, the field, the knower of the field, wisdom, and what is to be known.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","prakriti","purusha","jnana"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":2,"order":491,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The body is observed; the knower is something else.","snippet":"The body is called the field, O Arjuna. Those who know it call the knower of the field the field-knower.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","body-awareness","observer","chapter-13"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":3,"order":492,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowing the field is incomplete without knowing the knower.","snippet":"Know Me as the knower in all fields, Arjuna. In my view, true knowledge is knowing the field and the knower of the field.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","field-and-knower","awareness","brahma-jnana"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":4,"order":493,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing begins by separating the field from the one who knows it.","snippet":"Listen to the field, its nature, its changes, its source, and the knower of the field, along with that knower\'s powers, in brief.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","viveka","field-and-knower","chapter-13"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":5,"order":494,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ancient sources converge on one disciplined way of seeing.","snippet":"This truth about the field and the knower has been sung in many ways by sages, in varied Vedic hymns, and in the reasoned, conclusive ver…","tags":["kshetra-kshetrajna","brahmasutra","rishis","vedas","inquiry"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":6,"order":495,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you call “me” is a changing system, not a single thing.","snippet":"The five great elements, ego, intellect, the unmanifest, the ten senses, the one mind, and the five sense-objects: this is the field in b…","tags":["kshetra","mahabhuta","ahankara","buddhi","indriya"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":7,"order":496,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your reactions belong to the field, not to the knower.","snippet":"Desire, aversion, pleasure, pain, the body, consciousness, and steadiness: this field, together with its changes, is briefly described.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","iccha","dvesha","sukha-duhkha"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":8,"order":497,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True strength is quiet discipline, not self-display.","snippet":"Absence of pride, absence of pretence, nonviolence, forgiveness, simplicity, service to the teacher, purity, steadiness, and self-control.","tags":["ahimsa","arjava","shaucha","amaanitvam","self-control"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":9,"order":498,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when desire stops dressing suffering as reward.","snippet":"Dispassion toward sense objects, absence of ego, and constant seeing of the fault in birth, death, old age, and disease.","tags":["vairagya","ahamkara","indriya-vishaya","jaramrityu","duhkha-darshana"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":10,"order":499,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clinging fades; the mind stays level.","snippet":"Freedom from attachment to sons, wife, home, and the like; and constant evenness of mind in desired and undesired events.","tags":["asakti","anabhisvanga","samachittatva","ishthanishta","kshetra-kshetrajna"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":11,"order":500,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True devotion stays with one center and loses interest in the crowd.","snippet":"Undivided devotion to me, a love that does not waver, delight in solitude, and no attraction to crowds.","tags":["ananyayoga","bhakti","solitude","crowds","seclusion"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":12,"order":501,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowledge is seeing reality steadily; everything else is confusion.","snippet":"Constant awareness of the inner reality, and seeing the supreme reality as the meaning of true understanding—this is called knowledge; wh…","tags":["adhyatma","tattva-jnana","viveka","avidya","kshetra-kshetrajna"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":13,"order":502,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest reality frees you precisely because it outgrows every label.","snippet":"I will now tell you what is to be known. Knowing it, one attains freedom. It is beginningless supreme reality, beyond existence and nonex…","tags":["kshetra-kshetrajna","brahman","amrita","anadi","sat-asat"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":14,"order":503,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What seems separate is already filled with the supreme reality.","snippet":"The supreme reality has hands and feet everywhere, eyes, heads, and faces everywhere, and ears everywhere. It pervades all things and sta…","tags":["sarvatra","kshetrajna","omnipresence","vishvavyapi","bhagavan"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":15,"order":504,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What sustains everything is beyond the senses that perceive it.","snippet":"The supreme reality has no senses, yet illumines every sense-object. It is detached, supports all beings, beyond the three qualities, and…","tags":["kshetrajna","gunas","nirguna","sarvabhrit","indriya"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":16,"order":505,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What seems distant is already within everything.","snippet":"The supreme reality is inside and outside all beings, moving and unmoving. Because it is subtle, it cannot be known; it is far away and n…","tags":["antaryamin","sarvavyapi","sukshma","bhutanam","paratva"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":17,"order":506,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Separation is only appearance; the many are held by one.","snippet":"Undivided among beings, it appears divided. Know it as the one who bears, devours, and creates all beings.","tags":["kshetrajna","nonduality","bhuta-bharta","unity-in-diversity","manifestation"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":18,"order":507,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What illumines everything is already nearest to you.","snippet":"It is the light of all lights, beyond darkness. It is knowledge, the knowable, reached through knowledge, and abiding in every heart.","tags":["kshetrajna","jyotisham","hṛdaya","tamas","jñeya"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":19,"order":508,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear understanding becomes transformation when devotion receives it.","snippet":"Thus, field, knowledge, and the knowable have been explained briefly. My devotee, understanding this, attains my state.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","madbhava","bhakta","jnana"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":20,"order":509,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Change belongs to nature; awareness is not caught in it.","snippet":"Know both Prakriti and Purusha to be beginningless, and know the modifications and qualities to arise from Prakriti.","tags":["prakriti","purusha","gunas","kshetra","kshetrajna"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":21,"order":510,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action belongs to nature; experience belongs to the one who knows.","snippet":"Nature is said to be the cause of the body, the senses, and action. The inner being is said to be the cause of experiencing pleasure and …","tags":["prakriti","purusha","kshetra-kshetrajna","doership","bhoktṛtva"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":22,"order":511,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Attachment to changing qualities keeps the cycle of birth going.","snippet":"The inner being, situated in nature, experiences the qualities born of nature. Attachment to those qualities causes birth in good and bad…","tags":["prakriti","gunas","gुणसंग","punarjanma","kshetrajna"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":23,"order":512,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Identity is borrowed from the body; the true self stands beyond it.","snippet":"The inner self becomes the witness, consent-giver, supporter, enjoyer, and great lord through its relation with the body. Yet in its true…","tags":["kshetrajna","purusha","prakriti","deha","upadrashta"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":24,"order":513,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing frees you while life still continues.","snippet":"Whoever thus knows the purusha and prakriti together with the qualities is not born again, even while living and acting in every way.","tags":["kshetra-kshetrajna","prakriti","purusha","gunas","rebirth"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":25,"order":514,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The same realization opens through different disciplines.","snippet":"Some realize the true self within through meditation on the self. Others through clear discernment and yoga, and still others through the…","tags":["kshetrajna","dhyana","sankhya","karmayoga","atman"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":26,"order":515,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devoted listening can carry a person beyond fear and mortality.","snippet":"Others do not know these paths, but they worship by hearing from others. Even they cross beyond death if they listen with devotion.","tags":["shruti","upasana","shraddha","moksha","guru-vakya"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":27,"order":516,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All forms arise from the meeting of awareness and changing nature.","snippet":"O best among the Bharatas, know that whatever comes into being, moving or unmoving, arises from the union of the field and the knower of …","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","samyoga","manifestation","field-and-knower"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":28,"order":517,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Real seeing notices one imperishable presence in every changing form.","snippet":"One who sees the supreme being equally present in all beings, imperishable amid the perishing, truly sees.","tags":["kshetra-kshetrajna","samadarshana","parameshvara","avinashi","nonduality"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":29,"order":518,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing unity everywhere ends the violence that returns to yourself.","snippet":"Seeing the divine equally everywhere, a person does not wound the true self by the true self, and reaches the highest state.","tags":["kshetrajna","sarvatrasamadarshana","paramgati","atmavihimsa","ishvara"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":30,"order":519,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when you stop claiming every action as yours.","snippet":"One who sees all actions as being done only by nature, and sees the true self as the non-doer, sees rightly.","tags":["prakriti","akartā","kshetra","kshetrajna","non-doership"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":31,"order":520,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Many beings are one reality seen through different forms.","snippet":"When one sees all beings as rooted in one nature and all expansion arising from that source, one attains the supreme reality.","tags":["kshetra-kshetrajna","brahman","unity-in-diversity","anupashyati","field-and-knower"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":32,"order":521,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you are remains unstained, even while life moves through you.","snippet":"O son of Kunti, this supreme self is beginningless, beyond the gunas, and imperishable. Though abiding in the body, it does not act and i…","tags":["kshetrajna","nirguna","avyaya","anadi","body-consciousness"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":33,"order":522,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is everywhere cannot be stained by what changes.","snippet":"As all-pervading space is not tainted because of its subtlety, so the self, present in every body, is not tainted.","tags":["kshetra-kshetrajna","atma","akasha","nonattachment","body-consciousness"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":34,"order":523,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Awareness illuminates everything without being touched by what it sees.","snippet":"As one sun illuminates this whole world, so the knower of the field illuminates the whole field, O Bharata.","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","atma","sun-metaphor","field-and-knower"]},{"chapter":13,"verse":35,"order":524,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing separates you from what changes and opens the way beyond it.","snippet":"In this way, those who know the distinction between the field and the knower of the field with the eye of wisdom, and who know release fr…","tags":["kshetra","kshetrajna","viveka","prakriti","moksha"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":1,"order":525,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Some knowledge does not inform you; it completes you.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: I will speak again of the highest knowledge, the best of all knowledge. Knowing this, all sages have reached the s…","tags":["gunatraya","parama-jnana","muni","siddhi","krishna-teaching"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":2,"order":526,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True understanding makes beginning and ending stop ruling you.","snippet":"Having taken refuge in this knowledge, they attain my likeness. They are not born at creation, and they are not troubled at dissolution.","tags":["gunatraya","sarga","pralaya","mama-sadharmya","krishna-jnana"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":3,"order":527,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All birth comes from a source beyond personal control.","snippet":"O Bharata, my primal nature is the womb; I place the seed in it. From that, all beings are born.","tags":["prakriti","creation","garbha","jagat-janma","cosmic-origin"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":4,"order":528,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All forms arise from one source, and the divine gives them life.","snippet":"O son of Kunti, in all forms of birth, the material nature is the womb, and I am the seed-giving father.","tags":["prakriti","mahat-brahma","yoni","seed","cosmic-origin"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":5,"order":529,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Nature\'s three forces keep the changeless one identified with the body.","snippet":"Arjuna, the three qualities of nature—sattva, rajas, and tamas—bind the imperishable inner being to the body.","tags":["gunas","prakriti","dehin","embodiment","bondage"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":6,"order":530,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even clarity becomes bondage when you cling to its pleasure.","snippet":"Among those qualities, sattva—because it is pure and luminous and free from affliction—binds the embodied being through attachment to hap…","tags":["sattva","gunas","attachment-to-knowledge","attachment-to-happiness","gunatraya"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":7,"order":531,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Craving turns action into a chain.","snippet":"Know rajas as passion-born, born of craving and attachment. It binds the embodied being through attachment to action, O son of Kunti.","tags":["gunas","rajas","trishna","sanga","karma-asakti"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":8,"order":532,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Confusion binds most through laziness, not force.","snippet":"Arjuna, know tamas to be born of ignorance and deluding all embodied beings. It binds them through heedlessness, laziness, and sleep.","tags":["tamas","gunatraya","pramada","alasya","nidra"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":9,"order":533,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Each force traps you in a different way: comfort, activity, or blindness.","snippet":"Sattva binds through pleasure, rajas through action, and tamas, covering knowledge, binds through negligence.","tags":["gunas","sattva","rajas","tamas","pramada"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":10,"order":534,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What dominates the mind is temporary, not who you are.","snippet":"Arjuna, when rajas and tamas are subdued, sattva rises. When sattva and tamas are subdued, rajas rises. When sattva and rajas are subdued…","tags":["gunas","sattva","rajas","tamas","mental-states"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":11,"order":535,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Inner brightness is the sign that clarity is taking over.","snippet":"When light, clarity, and understanding arise in all the gates of this body, know that sattva has grown strong.","tags":["sattva","gunas","prakasha","viveka","inner clarity"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":12,"order":536,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Restless wanting multiplies action, but never settles the mind.","snippet":"O best of the Bharatas, when rajas grows, greed, activity, the beginning of actions, restlessness, and desire arise.","tags":["rajas","lobha","spṛha","restlessness","gunas"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":13,"order":537,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Darkness does not stay still; it breeds neglect and confusion.","snippet":"O descendant of Kuru, when tamas grows strong, darkness, inertia, negligence, and delusion arise.","tags":["gunas","tamas","inertia","delusion","negligence"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":14,"order":538,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A clear state carries consciousness toward a clearer destination.","snippet":"When sattva is predominant at death, the embodied being reaches the pure worlds of the wise.","tags":["sattva","gunas","death","afterlife","clarity"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":15,"order":539,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your strongest tendency decides the shape of your next beginning.","snippet":"A being who dies in rajas is born among those attached to action. A being who dies in tamas is born among deluded forms.","tags":["gunas","rajas","tamas","rebirth","karma-phala"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":16,"order":540,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action carries its own flavor of result.","snippet":"The result of wholesome action is pure and clear; the result of rajasic action is suffering; the result of tamasic action is ignorance an…","tags":["gunas","sattva","rajas","tamas","karma-phala"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":17,"order":541,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your mental weather has causes: clarity, craving, and confusion each grow from different qualities.","snippet":"From sattva comes knowledge; from rajas, greed; from tamas, negligence, delusion, and ignorance.","tags":["gunas","sattva","rajas","tamas","greed"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":18,"order":542,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your inner quality decides the direction of your life.","snippet":"Those established in sattva go upward; those in rajas remain in the middle; those in the lowest movement of tamas go downward.","tags":["gunas","sattva","rajas","tamas","higher-lower-states"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":19,"order":543,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when you stop mistaking qualities for a personal doer.","snippet":"When the seer understands that no doer exists apart from the three qualities, and knows the divine nature beyond them, that seer reaches …","tags":["gunas","kartaa","viveka","prakriti","madbhava"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":20,"order":544,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when the three qualities no longer define you.","snippet":"The embodied one who rises beyond these three qualities, which arise from the body, is freed from birth, death, old age, and sorrow, and …","tags":["gunas","janma-mrtyu-jara-duhkha","amritam","dehi","moksha"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":21,"order":545,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Real freedom must be visible, livable, and learnable.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Lord, by what signs is a person known who has gone beyond these three qualities? How does such a person behave, and how do…","tags":["gunas","gunasatita","arjuna-prashna","triguna","vairagya"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":22,"order":546,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when changing states stop controlling your response.","snippet":"Krishna said: O Arjuna, the one who has gone beyond the three gunas does not hate light, activity, or confusion when they appear, and doe…","tags":["gunas","equanimity","vairagya","mohah","inner states"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":23,"order":547,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when movement happens, but identity does not.","snippet":"One who remains like an indifferent witness, unmoved by the three qualities, stands firm and does not stir, knowing only that the qualiti…","tags":["gunas","gunatita","equanimity","witness-consciousness","inner-stability"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":24,"order":548,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness means nothing external gets to decide your center.","snippet":"The steady one remains equal in pleasure and pain, in a clod of earth, a stone, and gold; equal toward the liked and the disliked, toward…","tags":["equanimity","gunas","samatva","praise-blame","detachment"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":25,"order":549,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when praise, blame, and personal impulse lose their power over you.","snippet":"The steady one is equal in honor and dishonor, equal toward friend and foe, and has abandoned all undertakings. Such a person is called b…","tags":["gunas","equanimity","honor-dishonor","friend-foe","renunciation-of-action"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":26,"order":550,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady devotion can carry you beyond the forces that shape ordinary life.","snippet":"Whoever serves Me with unwavering devotion transcends these qualities and becomes fit for union with the supreme reality.","tags":["bhakti-yoga","gunas","brahma-bhuyaya","avyabhichari-bhakti","transcendence"]},{"chapter":14,"verse":27,"order":551,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"All ultimate freedom rests in Krishna, not apart from him.","snippet":"For I am the foundation of Brahman, of immortality, of the imperishable, of eternal dharma, and of unending bliss.","tags":["brahman","amrita","avyaya","shashvata-dharma","anantika-sukha"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":1,"order":552,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Understanding the world-tree is the beginning of true understanding.","snippet":"The Blessed Lord said: They speak of the imperishable banyan-like tree of the world, with roots above and branches below. The Vedas are i…","tags":["ashvattha","world-tree","vedas","upside-down-tree","chapter-15"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":2,"order":553,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Craving and action keep the world-tree growing in every direction.","snippet":"Its branches spread below, above, and across. They are nourished by the three qualities, with sense-pleasures as their shoots. In the hum…","tags":["ashvattha","gunas","indriya-vishaya","karma-bandha","samsara"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":3,"order":554,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What traps you has no fixed form; detachment cuts it cleanly.","snippet":"Its form is not perceived here as it truly is: it has no beginning, no end, and no fixed base. Cut down this deeply rooted ashvattha tree…","tags":["ashvattha","vairagya","detachment","impermanence","world-tree"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":4,"order":555,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The final refuge is a state where return itself stops.","snippet":"Therefore one should seek that supreme state, reaching which one does not return again. I take refuge in that original Person from whom t…","tags":["purushottama","paramam padam","anavrtti","prapatti","samsara"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":5,"order":556,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when pride, craving, and inner division fall away.","snippet":"Free from pride and delusion, victorious over attachment, ever rooted in the true self, desireless, and beyond the opposites of pleasure …","tags":["purushottama","moksha","vairagya","dvandva","adhyatma"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":6,"order":557,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest home is beyond every ordinary light and beyond return.","snippet":"The sun, moon, and fire do not illumine that place. Having reached it, one does not return. That supreme abode is Mine.","tags":["parama-dhama","purushottama","returnlessness","transcendence","cosmic-light"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":7,"order":558,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is eternal gets pulled around by what changes.","snippet":"The embodied being in this world is my eternal part, yet it draws the mind and the five senses, which rest in nature.","tags":["purushottama","jiva","manas","indriyas","prakriti"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":8,"order":559,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The body changes, but the carried pattern moves on.","snippet":"Just as the wind carries fragrance from its source, the embodied being carries the mind and senses into a new body.","tags":["punarjanma","manas","indriya","dehantara","atma-gati"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":9,"order":560,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Experience passes through mind and senses; it does not define the true self.","snippet":"Taking hold of the mind, the inner being experiences objects through the ears, eyes, skin, tongue, and nose.","tags":["indriyas","manas","pratyaksha","kshetra-kshetrajna","purusha"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":10,"order":561,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What changes is seen by the wise; the true self is not what moves.","snippet":"The deluded do not see the inner being departing, staying, or enjoying the world through the qualities. Those with the eye of understandi…","tags":["purushottama","gunas","jiva","knowledge-eye","body-identification"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":11,"order":562,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Seeing the supreme reality depends on inner purification, not effort alone.","snippet":"The striving yogis see this supreme reality abiding in themselves. The unrefined and thoughtless, even while striving, do not see it.","tags":["purushottama","antarshuddhi","yogi","clear-seeing","inner-realization"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":12,"order":563,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every brightness in the world points back to one source.","snippet":"The radiance in the sun, the moon, and the fire is Mine alone.","tags":["vibhuti","radiance","surya","chandra","agni"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":13,"order":564,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Life is nourished from within by the same presence that holds it together.","snippet":"Entering the earth, I sustain all beings with my power. Becoming the moon of life-giving essence, I nourish all plants.","tags":["vibhuti","somo rasatmakah","plant nourishment","earth support","krishna omnipresence"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":14,"order":565,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The divine is already working inside your body as life itself.","snippet":"I become the digestive fire within living beings, joined with the outgoing and incoming breaths, and digest the four kinds of food.","tags":["vaisvanara","digestive fire","prana-apana","embodied divinity","ch15"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":15,"order":566,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deepest knowing comes from the one already dwelling within every heart.","snippet":"I dwell in the hearts of all beings. Memory, knowledge, and removal of doubt come from Me. I am the one known through all the Vedas, the …","tags":["hridaya","smriti","vedanta","vedavid","inner guidance"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":16,"order":567,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What changes is not the whole of you.","snippet":"In this world, there are two kinds of beings: the perishable and the imperishable. All embodied beings are perishable; the steadfast one …","tags":["kshara","akshara","kootastha","purusha","impermanence"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":17,"order":568,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even the imperishable witness is not the final reality.","snippet":"The Supreme Self is beyond both the perishable and the imperishable. The imperishable ruler enters the three worlds and sustains them all.","tags":["purushottama","paramatma","lokatraya","avyaya","kshara-akshara"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":18,"order":569,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The highest reality lies beyond both change and permanence.","snippet":"I am beyond the perishable and even beyond the imperishable. Therefore, I am known in the world and in the Vedas as Purushottama, the Sup…","tags":["purushottama","kshara","akshara","paramatma","chapter-15"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":19,"order":570,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clear seeing of the Supreme Self becomes total devotion.","snippet":"Arjuna, the one who is free from confusion and knows Me as the Supreme Self, worships Me with all his being.","tags":["purushottama","bhajana","clear-seeing","paramatma","bhakti"]},{"chapter":15,"verse":20,"order":571,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Secret knowledge makes a person complete.","snippet":"O sinless Arjuna, thus this most secret teaching has been spoken by Me. Knowing this, a person becomes wise and has accomplished all that…","tags":["purushottama","guhyatama","krtakrtya","jnana","moksha"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":1,"order":572,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action starts with disciplined character.","snippet":"Fearlessness, purity of mind, steadfastness in the yoga of knowledge, generosity, self-control, sacrifice, study of the sacred texts, aus…","tags":["daivi-sampad","fearlessness","self-control","swadhyaya","tapas"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":2,"order":573,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A noble character is proven by how gently it reacts.","snippet":"Nonviolence, truthfulness, freedom from anger, renunciation, inner calm, absence of slander, compassion for all beings, freedom from gree…","tags":["ahimsa","satya","akrodha","dainya","apaisunam"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":3,"order":574,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True strength looks like forgiveness, steadiness, and no need to dominate.","snippet":"Splendor, forgiveness, steadiness, purity, absence of hostility, and lack of pride belong to the one born with divine qualities, O Bharata.","tags":["daivi-sampad","forgiveness","humility","steadiness","purity"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":4,"order":575,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"False pride and cruelty reveal a nature already turned away from wisdom.","snippet":"O son of Pritha, hypocrisy, arrogance, self-importance, anger, harshness, and ignorance are the marks of one born with demonic qualities.","tags":["asuri-sampad","darpa","abhimana","parushya","krodha"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":5,"order":576,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom grows from one kind of character; bondage grows from another.","snippet":"The divine nature leads to freedom; the demonic nature leads to bondage. Do not grieve, Pandava. You are born with the divine nature.","tags":["daivi-sampad","asuri-sampad","freedom-bondage","ego","chapter-16"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":6,"order":577,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Human life divides by inner orientation, not by appearance.","snippet":"In this world there are two kinds of beings: the divine and the shadowed. I have already described the divine in detail; now listen to th…","tags":["daivi-sampad","asuri-sampad","chapter-16","human-nature","moral-classification"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":7,"order":578,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Without discernment, conduct collapses and truth disappears.","snippet":"People of a shadowed nature do not know what should be pursued and what should be withdrawn from. In them, there is no purity, no noble c…","tags":["asuri-prakriti","pravritti-nivritti","shaucha","achara","satya"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":8,"order":579,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Cynical explanations of life can become a permission slip for harmful action.","snippet":"They say the world is unreal, without foundation, and without a ruling order, born only from the union of male and female. They say desir…","tags":["asuric","nihilism","desire","worldview","adharma"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":9,"order":580,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"False vision turns strength into destruction.","snippet":"Holding this view, deluded people with ruined discernment and fierce actions arise only to destroy the world.","tags":["asuri-prakriti","alpabuddhi","ugrakarma","false-view","destructive-action"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":10,"order":581,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Endless wanting turns the mind into a home for delusion.","snippet":"Taking refuge in desires that can never be filled, filled with hypocrisy, pride, and intoxication, they wander under delusion, holding on…","tags":["kama","dambha","mana","mada","moha"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":11,"order":582,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Endless wanting turns life into a tunnel with no horizon.","snippet":"They take refuge in endless worries that last until death, live only for acquiring and enjoying things, and decide that this is all there…","tags":["kama","aparimeya-chinta","asuri-sampad","bhogaparayana","artha-sanchaya"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":12,"order":583,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire and anger turn ambition into injustice.","snippet":"Bound by hundreds of cords of hope, driven by desire and anger, they strive to gather wealth unjustly for the enjoyment of desires.","tags":["kama","krodha","arthasanchaya","ashapasha","adharma"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":13,"order":584,"speaker":"Unknown","essence":"Possession feeds appetite when the mind mistakes gain for completion.","snippet":"This much I have gained today; I will get this desire fulfilled. This wealth is mine now, and more will be mine again.","tags":["lobha","artha","possessiveness","greed-cycle","asuri-sampad"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":14,"order":585,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ego turns achievement into delusion and mistakes possession for mastery.","snippet":"That enemy has been slain by me, and I will slay the others too. I am the lord, I enjoy, I am accomplished, powerful, and happy.","tags":["ahamkara","asuri-sampad","ego","delusion","arrogance"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":15,"order":586,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Pride turns abundance into delusion and makes more wanting feel justified.","snippet":"We are rich, surrounded by many people. Who is equal to us? We will sacrifice, give, and enjoy. Deluded by ignorance, they think this way.","tags":["ahankara","asuric-mind","greed","status","self-deception"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":16,"order":587,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire scatters the mind, and confusion turns that scattering into a fall.","snippet":"Deluded by many desires, trapped in the net of confusion, and deeply attached to pleasures, people fall into a lower realm of misery.","tags":["kama","mohajala","attachment","delusion","mind-scatter"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":17,"order":588,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Pride can hollow out sacred action until only appearance remains.","snippet":"Self-important, stubborn, drunk on wealth and praise, they perform ritual in name only, with pretence and without proper method.","tags":["ahamkara","dambha","ritual","wealth-pride","false-piety"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":18,"order":589,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ego makes you fight the divine presence you carry yourself.","snippet":"Those who take refuge in ego, force, arrogance, desire, and anger hate Me, who dwell in their own bodies and in the bodies of others, and…","tags":["ahankara","darpa","kama","krodha","fault-finding"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":19,"order":590,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Repeated hatred drives a person into worse and worse forms of existence.","snippet":"I cast those hateful, cruel, and vile people again and again into demonic births.","tags":["asuri-bhava","demonic-birth","hatred","cruelty","lower-rebirth"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":20,"order":591,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Repeated delusion keeps pulling a person farther from the divine.","snippet":"Those deluded beings, born again and again into shadowed births, never reach me and sink into a lower state.","tags":["asuri-yoni","delusion","rebirth","adhama-gati","chapter-16"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":21,"order":592,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Three inner forces open the way to ruin; dropping them protects the self.","snippet":"Desire, anger, and greed are the three gates of ruin. Abandon these three.","tags":["kama","krodha","lobha","self-mastery","adharma"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":22,"order":593,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom from the three dark impulses opens the way to your highest good.","snippet":"Freed from these three gates of darkness, a person acts for their own good and reaches the highest state.","tags":["trividha-dvara","kama","krodha","lobha","sreyas"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":23,"order":594,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Impulse cannot deliver what it promises.","snippet":"Whoever sets aside scripture and acts on desire alone does not attain perfection, happiness, or the highest state.","tags":["shastravidhi","kamakaratah","desire","discipline","adharma"]},{"chapter":16,"verse":24,"order":595,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Impulse cannot judge action; a higher standard must.","snippet":"Therefore, scripture is your authority for deciding what should be done and what should not be done. Knowing the duties laid out in scrip…","tags":["shastra-pramana","kartavya","akartavya","dharma","right-action"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":1,"order":596,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Faith alone does not reveal its quality; the motive beneath it does.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O Krishna, what is the standing of those who worship with faith while setting aside the rules of scripture? Is it sattvic, r…","tags":["shraddha","sattva-rajas-tamas","scriptural authority","worship","inquiry"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":2,"order":597,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Faith takes the shape of the nature beneath it.","snippet":"The faith of embodied beings is born of their nature. It is of three kinds: sattvic, rajasic, and tamasic. Listen to this.","tags":["shraddha","sattva","rajas","tamas","gunas"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":3,"order":598,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Trust is not just held; it becomes the person.","snippet":"O Bharata, each person\'s trust matches their inner nature. A person is made of trust; whatever trust he holds, that is what he becomes.","tags":["shraddha","inner disposition","character formation","bhakti","guna"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":4,"order":599,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Faith reveals itself in what each person chooses to revere.","snippet":"The sattvic worship radiant beings; the rajasic worship yakshas and rakshasas; the tamasic worship spirits and hosts of the dead.","tags":["shraddha","sattva","rajas","tamas","worship"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":5,"order":600,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Harsh effort without right guidance can deepen ego instead of cleansing it.","snippet":"People who perform harsh austerities without scriptural guidance, driven by vanity, ego, desire, attachment, and stubbornness, are not pu…","tags":["tapas","dambha","ahankara","kamaraga","asuri-sampad"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":6,"order":601,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Harshness is not holiness when it destroys the body and ignores what lives within.","snippet":"Those who are ignorant and perform terrible austerities without scriptural guidance, wasting away the body’s elements and Me dwelling wit…","tags":["asuric","tapas","shastravihita","ahankara","self-harm"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":7,"order":602,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Even sacred actions differ; their inner quality decides their worth.","snippet":"Food, sacrifice, charity, and austerity are each of three kinds. Listen to these distinctions.","tags":["sattva","rajas","tamas","ahara","yajna"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":8,"order":603,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Wholesome food quietly builds the conditions for a steadier life.","snippet":"Foods that increase life, purity, strength, health, happiness, and cheerfulness, and are tasty, smooth, firm, and pleasing, are dear to t…","tags":["sattvic food","ahara","diet discipline","health","clarity"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":9,"order":604,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What excites the senses can quietly produce suffering.","snippet":"Bitter, sour, salty, overly hot, pungent, dry, and burning foods are dear to the passionate person. They bring pain, grief, and illness.","tags":["rajasic-food","ahara","sattva-rajas-tamas","dietary-habits","sense-stimulation"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":10,"order":605,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What you repeatedly choose to consume reveals the heaviness within.","snippet":"Food that is half-cooked, tasteless, foul-smelling, stale, leftover, and impure is dear to people ruled by tamas.","tags":["tamas","ahara","stale-food","indriya","shraddha"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":11,"order":606,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action becomes pure when reward stops being the reason.","snippet":"A sacrifice performed according to scriptural rule by people without desire for reward, with the mind settled on “it must be done,” is sa…","tags":["yajna","sattva","nishkama","scriptural-duty","offering"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":12,"order":607,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"An offering for reward or applause loses its purity.","snippet":"But, best of the Bharatas, know that sacrifice to be rajasic when it is performed for reward or for show.","tags":["rajasic-yajna","abhisandha","dambha","shraddhatraya","motivation"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":13,"order":608,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ritual without trust becomes empty and heavy.","snippet":"They call a sacrifice dark when it lacks scriptural rule, food offering, mantra, fee, and trust.","tags":["shraddha","yajna","tamas","mantra","dakshina"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":14,"order":609,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The body itself can become a disciplined offering.","snippet":"Worship of the radiant beings, the wise, the teacher, and the enlightened; purity, simplicity, celibacy, and non-violence — these are cal…","tags":["tapas","brahmacharya","ahimsa","shaucha","arjava"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":15,"order":610,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Speech becomes discipline when it tells the truth without creating harm.","snippet":"Speech that does not agitate, is truthful, pleasant, and beneficial, together with study and practice, is called austerity of speech.","tags":["vagmaya-tapas","satya","ahimsa","svadhyaya","speech-discipline"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":16,"order":611,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A trained mind is its own austerity.","snippet":"Serenity of mind, gentleness, silence, self-control, and purity of feeling are called mental austerity.","tags":["tapas","manas","self-restraint","mental-discipline","sattva"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":17,"order":612,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True discipline is clean only when reward is no longer the motive.","snippet":"That threefold discipline of body, speech, and mind, performed with supreme trust and without craving results, is called sattvic.","tags":["shraddha","tapas","sattva","nishkama","body-speech-mind"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":18,"order":613,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Practice for applause collapses into instability.","snippet":"Austerity done for honor, praise, and worship, or with a show of display, is said to be rajasic here. It gives unstable, temporary results.","tags":["rajasic-tapas","satkara","mana","puja","dambha"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":19,"order":614,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Pain imposed in ignorance only deepens confusion.","snippet":"Austerity done with foolish stubbornness, by torturing oneself or harming others, is called tamasic.","tags":["tapas","tamasic","self-harm","austerity","discipline"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":20,"order":615,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Giving becomes pure when nothing is being bought in return.","snippet":"A gift given with the feeling that giving is a duty, offered to a worthy person at the right place and time, is called sattvic.","tags":["dana","sattvika-dana","anupakarine","tyaga","shraddha"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":21,"order":616,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A gift becomes lesser the moment it starts asking for something back.","snippet":"But charity given in return, or for a desired result, and given grudgingly, is said to be rajasic.","tags":["dana","rajas","pratyupakara","phala-iccha","seva"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":22,"order":617,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"A gift can become degrading when respect is missing.","snippet":"Charity given at the wrong place and time, to an unworthy recipient, without respect and with contempt, is called tamasic.","tags":["danam","tamasic","charity","respect","recipient"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":23,"order":618,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sacred action matters because it points beyond itself to what is real.","snippet":"Om, Tat, and Sat are the three names by which the supreme reality is known. By that, the Vedas, the priests, and the sacrifices were esta…","tags":["om","tat","sat","yajna","vedas"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":24,"order":619,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sacred action begins by naming the supreme reality first.","snippet":"Therefore, the ritual acts of sacrifice, charity, and austerity prescribed by scripture are always begun by uttering Om, for those who sp…","tags":["om","yajna","dana","tapas","brahmavadin"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":25,"order":620,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom deepens when action stops demanding a private return.","snippet":"Thinking “all this is for the supreme reality,” seekers of freedom perform many kinds of sacrifice, austerity, and giving without wanting…","tags":["yajna","tapas","dana","nishkama","moksha"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":26,"order":621,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What is real and worthy carries the mark of sat.","snippet":"O Partha, the word sat is used for existence itself, for noble being, and for praiseworthy action.","tags":["sat","sadvava","sadhubhava","praiseworthy-action","shraddha"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":27,"order":622,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steady offering makes ordinary action sacred.","snippet":"Steadfastness in sacrifice, austerity, and giving is called sat. Action done for that purpose is also called sat.","tags":["shraddha","sat","yajna","tapas","dana"]},{"chapter":17,"verse":28,"order":623,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Trust is what makes action real; without it, effort becomes empty.","snippet":"O Partha, sacrifice, charity, austerity, and any deed done without trust are called unreal. Its fruit exists neither here nor after death.","tags":["shraddha","homa","dana","tapas","sat-asat"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":1,"order":624,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Clear seeing begins with asking what must be separated.","snippet":"Arjuna said: O mighty-armed one, O master of the senses, O slayer of Kesi, I wish to know the distinct truth of renunciation and relinqui…","tags":["sannyasa","tyaga","viveka","chapter18","arjuna-question"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":2,"order":625,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Renunciation means releasing both craving and attachment to results.","snippet":"The wise call renunciation the giving up of desire-born actions. The discerning call renunciation the giving up of all results of action.","tags":["sannyasa","tyaga","karmaphala","nishkama","chapter-18"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":3,"order":626,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Renunciation is not simple refusal; some actions must remain.","snippet":"Some wise people say all action should be abandoned as flawed. Others say sacrifice, giving, and disciplined effort should not be abandoned.","tags":["tyaga","sannyasa","yajna","dana","tapas"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":4,"order":627,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Renunciation is not one thing; it has distinct forms.","snippet":"Arjuna, first hear my settled view on renunciation. Renunciation is said to be threefold.","tags":["tyaga","sannyasa","chapter-18","renunciation","discrimination"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":5,"order":628,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What purifies you should be done, not dropped.","snippet":"Sacrifice, giving, and disciplined effort should not be abandoned; they must be done. These three actions purify thoughtful people.","tags":["yajna","dana","tapas","renunciation","purification"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":6,"order":629,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action is complete only when desire for reward is dropped.","snippet":"Even these actions, and all other actions, should be done without attachment and without wanting their results. This is my settled and be…","tags":["nishkama-karma","tyaga","phala-tyaga","karma-yoga","krishna-teaching"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":7,"order":630,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Right action should not be abandoned just because it feels difficult.","snippet":"Abandoning prescribed action is not right. Giving it up in confusion is called tamasic.","tags":["tyaga","tamasic","niyata-karma","renunciation","dharma"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":8,"order":631,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Fearful withdrawal is not freedom; it is avoidance wearing a noble name.","snippet":"If someone gives up action thinking it is only suffering and fearing bodily strain, that renunciation is passionate, and it brings no fru…","tags":["tyaga","rajas","avoidance","karma","fear"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":9,"order":632,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Renunciation means doing what must be done without gripping the result.","snippet":"Arjuna, when fixed duty is done as only duty, without clinging to results, that renunciation is called sattvic.","tags":["tyaga","nishkama","karma yoga","attachment","fixed duty"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":10,"order":633,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom means neither resisting the hard nor craving the pleasant.","snippet":"One who neither rejects unwholesome action nor clings to wholesome action is a wise renunciate, free of doubt and established in clear se…","tags":["vairagya","tyaga","sattva","doubtlessness","clinging"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":11,"order":634,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom begins when action continues and attachment stops.","snippet":"For embodied beings, total renunciation of action is impossible. Therefore, one who renounces the fruits of action is called a renunciant.","tags":["tyaga","karmaphala","sannyasa","vairagya","action-without-attachment"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":12,"order":635,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The chain of action ends when desire for its fruit ends.","snippet":"For those who do not renounce the fruits of action, action produces three kinds of results—pleasant, unpleasant, and mixed—even after dea…","tags":["karma-phala","tyaga","sannyasa","renunciation","afterlife"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":13,"order":636,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action has many causes; the ego is not the whole story.","snippet":"O mighty-armed one, learn from Me these five causes, taught in the Sankhya system, for the accomplishment of all actions.","tags":["sankhya","karma","five causes","doership","action analysis"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":14,"order":637,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action has many causes, and no one factor owns the result.","snippet":"The field, the doer, the instruments, the many efforts, and the fifth factor, the unseen force, all shape every action.","tags":["karma","karta","karana","daiva","causation"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":15,"order":638,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every deed comes from five causes, not one isolated doer.","snippet":"Whatever action a person begins through body, speech, and mind—right or wrong—has these five causes.","tags":["five causes","agency","kartṛtva","body-speech-mind","sankhya"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":16,"order":639,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action has many causes; the pure self is not the lone doer.","snippet":"But one who sees only the pure self as the doer, even though these five causes are present, has not seen rightly; such a confused mind do…","tags":["kartā","five causes","akṛtabuddhi","agency","doership"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":17,"order":640,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Without egoic ownership, action leaves no stain.","snippet":"One who has no sense of separate self and whose understanding remains unstained does not kill, even by killing all these beings, and is n…","tags":["ahamkara","kartṛtva","karma-bandha","nishkama","doership"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":18,"order":641,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Action is a system, not a single ego doing everything.","snippet":"Knowledge, the object known, and the knower—these three drive action. Instrument, act, and actor—these three make up the whole of action.","tags":["trividha","karta","karana","karma-sangraha","jnana"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":19,"order":642,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every action, knower, and deed carries the mark of a quality.","snippet":"In the analysis of the three qualities, knowledge, action, and the doer are each said to be threefold. Listen now to these distinctions a…","tags":["gunas","triguna","karma","karta","jnana"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":20,"order":643,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True understanding sees one undivided reality inside every divided form.","snippet":"Know that knowledge to be sattvic by which one sees the one imperishable reality in all beings, undivided among the divided.","tags":["sattva","ekatva","bheda","avyaya","guna"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":21,"order":644,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Dividing everything into parts is not clarity; it is restless seeing.","snippet":"But know that knowledge as rajasic by which one sees many different beings as separate and distinct in all beings.","tags":["gunas","rajas","buddhi","separation","discriminating-mind"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":22,"order":645,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Small certainty can hide the least real understanding.","snippet":"But knowledge that clings to one body as if it were the whole, without reason, without truth, and petty, is called dark.","tags":["gunas","tamas","atattvartha","buddhi","partial-knowledge"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":23,"order":646,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The purest action asks for nothing back.","snippet":"Action that is guided by duty, free from attachment, and done without craving results is called sattvic.","tags":["sattva","nishkama-karma","attachment","raaga-dvesha","duty"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":24,"order":647,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Desire and ego turn action restless, even when it looks productive.","snippet":"But action done with desire for pleasure, or with ego, or with great strain, is said to be rajasic.","tags":["rajas","desire-driven-action","ahamkara","strain","guna-triad"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":25,"order":648,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Blind action begins where clear seeing is absent.","snippet":"Action begun in delusion, ignoring its consequences, harm, and one’s own capacity, is called tamasic.","tags":["tamasic-karma","delusion","consequences","ahankara","action-quality"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":26,"order":649,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Pure action leaves the ego out and stays calm in victory or defeat.","snippet":"The doer who is free from attachment, free from ego, endowed with steadiness and enthusiasm, and unchanged by success or failure is calle…","tags":["sattva","kartā","anahankara","dhriti","success-failure"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":27,"order":650,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Craving turns action into a chase for reward and emotional swing.","snippet":"The doer ruled by craving, chasing results, greedy, violent in nature, impure, and tossed by joy and sorrow is called passionate.","tags":["rajas","karmaphala","attachment","greed","doer"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":28,"order":651,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Dullness in the doer makes even action inert and harmful.","snippet":"A careless, crude, stubborn, deceitful, lazy, gloomy, and procrastinating doer is called tamasic.","tags":["tamas","tamasic","procrastination","laziness","deceit"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":29,"order":652,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Understanding and resolve differ by the quality that shapes them.","snippet":"O Dhananjaya, now hear the threefold distinctions of understanding and steadfastness according to the three qualities, fully and separate…","tags":["buddhi","dhriti","gunas","sattva-rajas-tamas","discrimination"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":30,"order":653,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True intelligence recognizes the difference between bondage and freedom.","snippet":"O Partha, the intellect that knows what leads forward and what withdraws, what should be done and not done, what is fear and fearlessness…","tags":["sattvic-buddhi","viveka","bandha-moksha","kartavya","fearlessness"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":31,"order":654,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Restless intelligence cannot tell duty from harm.","snippet":"Arjuna, the intellect that does not truly know right action and wrong action, duty and what should not be done, is rajasic.","tags":["rajasic-buddhi","duty","adharma","viveka","judgment"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":32,"order":655,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Darkness can make the wrong choice feel morally correct.","snippet":"The mind covered by darkness calls wrongdoing right and reverses everything.","tags":["tamasic-buddhi","adharma","buddhi","gunas","right-judgment"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":33,"order":656,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness becomes pure when it keeps the whole being aligned.","snippet":"O Partha, that steadfastness by which one holds steady the functions of mind, life-force, and senses through unwavering yoga is sattvic s…","tags":["dhriti","sattvika","manas","prana","indriya"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":34,"order":657,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Steadiness becomes restless when it is tied to reward.","snippet":"Arjuna, the steadiness that clings intensely to duty, pleasure, and wealth, while craving results, is passionate steadiness.","tags":["rajas","dhriti","attachment","phalakanksa","sattva-rajas"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":35,"order":658,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Clinging to fear and sorrow is not strength; it is tamasic inertia.","snippet":"The dull-minded one does not let go of sleep, fear, grief, sorrow, and pride. That steadfastness is tamasic, Arjuna.","tags":["tamasic","dhriti","gunas","fear","grief"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":36,"order":659,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True happiness begins as discipline and ends as relief.","snippet":"O best of the Bharatas, hear from me now about three kinds of happiness. The happiness that comes from practice, ends sorrow, and first f…","tags":["sattvic-sukha","abhyasa","gunas","duhkha-anta","mental-discipline"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":37,"order":660,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Lasting ease can begin as discomfort and end as release.","snippet":"That happiness is called sattvic, which seems like poison at first and like nectar in the end, born from clarity of the discerning mind a…","tags":["sattvic-sukha","buddhi-prasada","threefold-happiness","inner-clarity","tamas-rajas-sattva"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":38,"order":661,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"What feels sweetest first can become the harshest later.","snippet":"The pleasure that begins like nectar from contact between the senses and their objects, but ends like poison, is called rajasic pleasure.","tags":["rajasic-sukha","sense-contact","tamas","sattva","pleasure-and-pain"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":39,"order":662,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Pleasure that dulls you is not relief; it is confusion in disguise.","snippet":"That pleasure, born of sleep, laziness, and negligence, deludes the self at the beginning and at the end; it is called tamasic.","tags":["tamasic-sukha","sleep","laziness","pramada","gunas"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":40,"order":663,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"No state is free from the three qualities of nature.","snippet":"There is nothing on earth, in heaven, or among the radiant beings that is free from the three qualities born of nature.","tags":["triguna","prakriti","sattva-rajas-tamas","conditioned nature","field of action"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":41,"order":664,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your rightful work comes from your nature, not imitation.","snippet":"O scorcher of foes, the duties of priests, warriors, merchants, and workers are divided according to the qualities born of their nature.","tags":["varna","svabhava","guna","dharma","role"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":42,"order":665,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True duty begins as disciplined character, not public role.","snippet":"Self-restraint, control of the senses, austerity, purity, forgiveness, honesty, knowledge, realization, and faith in the supreme reality …","tags":["brahmin-dharma","shama","dama","tapas","shaucha"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":43,"order":666,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True strength serves, stands firm, and does not retreat.","snippet":"Valor, radiance, firmness, quick skill, never fleeing in battle, generosity, and leadership are the natural duties of a warrior.","tags":["kshatriya-dharma","apalayana","daakshya","shaurya","tejas"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":44,"order":667,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Every nature has its own rightful work.","snippet":"Farming, cattle-keeping, and trade are the natural work of the merchant class. Service to others is the natural work of the worker class.","tags":["varna","svabhava","dharma","vaishya","shudra"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":45,"order":668,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Fulfillment comes from living your own work, not someone else’s.","snippet":"A person devoted to their own work attains perfection. Listen as I explain how a person devoted to their own work reaches that perfection.","tags":["svakarma","siddhi","dharma","varna","personal-duty"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":46,"order":669,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Offering your work to the source of life turns ordinary action into fulfillment.","snippet":"By worshipping the one from whom all beings arise and by whom this whole world is pervaded, a person attains perfection through their own…","tags":["karma-yoga","swakarma","offering","svadharma","perfection"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":47,"order":670,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your imperfect duty is cleaner than a borrowed perfection.","snippet":"One\'s own duty, though imperfect, is better than another\'s duty well performed. Doing the work set by one\'s nature, a person does not inc…","tags":["svadharma","paradharma","nature-based-duty","karma-yoga","alignment"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":48,"order":671,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Your right work is still right, even when it is imperfect.","snippet":"O son of Kunti, one should not abandon one\'s natural duty, even if it has flaws. All undertakings are clouded by some defect, just as fir…","tags":["svadharma","natural-duty","imperfection","karma-yoga","action-flaws"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":49,"order":672,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom arrives when the mind stops reaching outward.","snippet":"One whose mind is detached everywhere, who has mastered the self, and who is free from craving attains the highest perfection of non-acti…","tags":["naishkarmya","sannyasa","vigrata-spṛha","jitatma","detachment"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":50,"order":673,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Knowledge has a highest point: direct arrival, not endless thinking.","snippet":"Listen to me briefly, O Arjuna, as I explain how one who has reached perfection attains the supreme reality, the highest culmination of k…","tags":["brahma","jnana","siddhi","nishtha","moksha"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":51,"order":674,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Purified resolve cuts the pull of craving and aversion.","snippet":"Endowed with purified understanding, holding the self steady with firm resolve, giving up sense-objects, and casting away attraction and …","tags":["buddhi","dhriti","indriya-nigraha","raga-dvesha","vairagya"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":52,"order":675,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom grows from deliberate simplicity and steady restraint.","snippet":"Dwelling in solitude, eating lightly, and controlling speech, body, and mind, one stays absorbed in meditation, grounded in non-attachment.","tags":["viviikta-seva","laghvashi","yatavak-kaya-manas","dhyana-yoga","vairagya"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":53,"order":676,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Peace begins when the sense of ownership ends.","snippet":"Free from ego, force, pride, desire, anger, and possession, one becomes peaceful, without “mine,” and fit for union with the supreme real…","tags":["ahamkara","mamakara","parigraha","vairagya","brahmabhuta"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":54,"order":677,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Freedom from craving makes room for the highest devotion.","snippet":"One who has become Brahman, serene in mind, grieves not and desires not. Equal toward all beings, that person attains supreme devotion to…","tags":["brahmabhuta","prasannatma","madbhakti","samah","vairagya"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":55,"order":678,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devoted love turns understanding into immediate nearness.","snippet":"Through devoted love, one truly knows Me as I am. Knowing Me in truth, one enters into Me at once.","tags":["bhakti","parabhakti","direct-knowledge","krishna","union"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":56,"order":679,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Continuous action and complete refuge can lead to the same unchanging state.","snippet":"A devotee who takes refuge in me, while always doing all actions, attains the eternal, imperishable state through my grace.","tags":["sharanagati","madvyapashraya","matprasada","nitya-karma","avyaya-pada"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":57,"order":680,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Hand over the action, and let the mind stay gathered there.","snippet":"With your mind, surrender all actions to Me. Take refuge in the discipline of clear understanding and remain constantly focused on Me.","tags":["sharanagati","buddhi-yoga","matparah","maccitta","karma-sannyasa"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":58,"order":681,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Grace opens the way; ego closes it.","snippet":"Centered in me, you will cross all obstacles through my grace. But if you do not listen because of ego, you will fall.","tags":["ahankara","prasad","sharanagati","ego-block","krishna-instruction"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":59,"order":682,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Ego cannot veto what your nature has already chosen.","snippet":"Relying on ego, you think, \'I will not fight.\' That resolve is false; your nature will drive you into battle.","tags":["ahankara","svabhava","kshatriya-dharma","battlefield","resistance"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":60,"order":683,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Resistance cannot cancel what your nature is already set to do.","snippet":"Bound by your own nature-born duty, you will do what you do not want to do in confusion. Even against your will, you will act.","tags":["svabhava","kshatriya-dharma","mohah","kurukshetra","self-deception"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":61,"order":684,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deeper mover is not your ego, and surrender begins there.","snippet":"O Arjuna, the Lord abides in the heart of all beings and, by His maya, causes all beings mounted on a body-machine to revolve according t…","tags":["maya","ishvara","hṛद्देश","surrender","body-machine"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":62,"order":685,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Wholehearted surrender opens the door to lasting peace.","snippet":"Surrender to the divine with your whole being, Arjuna. By that grace, you will reach supreme peace and the eternal abode.","tags":["sharanagati","krishna-prasada","eternal-abode","final-surrender","moksha-synthesis"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":63,"order":686,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True guidance ends by returning choice to you.","snippet":"Thus I have explained to you the most secret wisdom. Reflect on it fully, and then do as you wish.","tags":["sharanagati","final-teaching","free-choice","krishna-arjuna","moksha-sannyasa"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":64,"order":687,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"The deepest teaching is spoken as care, not command.","snippet":"Listen again to My most secret word. You are dear to Me, so I will speak for your good.","tags":["sharanagati","krishna-priya","guhyatama","final-teaching","bhakti"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":65,"order":688,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Wholehearted devotion becomes the shortest path home.","snippet":"Fix your mind on me, become my devotee, worship me, and bow to me. You will come to me; I promise you this truly, because you are dear to…","tags":["bhakti","surrender","manas","puja","namaskara"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":66,"order":689,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Total refuge ends the burden of fear.","snippet":"Abandon all duties and take refuge in Me alone. I will free you from all wrongdoing; do not grieve.","tags":["sharanagati","moksha","surrender","krishna","final-teaching"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":67,"order":690,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Deep truth must be shared only with those ready to receive it.","snippet":"Never speak this to one without discipline, one without devotion, one unwilling to listen, or one who finds fault with me.","tags":["parama-guhya","ashraddha","abhakti","shushrusha","krishna-upadesha"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":68,"order":691,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Devotion deepens when sacred truth is passed on.","snippet":"Whoever shares this supreme secret among my devotees, with devoted love for me, will surely come to me without doubt.","tags":["bhakti","parama-guhya","krishna","teaching","devotional-transmission"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":69,"order":692,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sharing this teaching becomes the highest form of devotion.","snippet":"Among all human beings, no one does what is more dear to me than he does. On this earth, no one will ever be dearer than he is.","tags":["bhakti","teaching-the-teaching","krishna-priya","parama-guhya","knowledge-sharing"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":70,"order":693,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Sincere study of this dialogue becomes worship itself.","snippet":"Whoever studies this sacred dialogue of ours will also worship me through the sacrifice of knowledge; that is my view.","tags":["jnana-yajna","sacred dialogue","study as worship","chapter 18","krishna-arjuna"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":71,"order":694,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"Trustful listening can open the door to freedom.","snippet":"Even a person who listens to this with trust and without fault-finding becomes free and reaches the auspicious realms earned by noble act…","tags":["shraddha","anasuya","listening","moksha","punyakarma"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":72,"order":695,"speaker":"Krishna","essence":"True listening should end confusion, not just collect words.","snippet":"O Partha, have you heard this with one-pointed mind? O Dhananjaya, has the delusion born of ignorance been destroyed in you?","tags":["one-pointed-mind","ignorance","delusion","kurukshetra","final-check"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":73,"order":696,"speaker":"Arjuna","essence":"Grace ends confusion and turns insight into obedience.","snippet":"Arjuna said: By your grace, O Achyuta, my delusion is destroyed and memory restored. I stand free of doubt and will do what you say.","tags":["arjuna","achyuta","krishna-grace","surrender","doubt-cleared"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":74,"order":697,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"A true dialogue can leave the listener shaken and changed.","snippet":"Sanjaya said: Thus I heard this wondrous, hair-raising dialogue between Vasudeva and the great-souled Partha.","tags":["sanjaya","dialogue","kurukshetra","arjuna","vasudeva"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":75,"order":698,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"The deepest teaching is received, not invented.","snippet":"By Vyasa\'s grace, I heard this supreme secret yoga directly from Krishna, the Lord of yoga, as he spoke it himself.","tags":["vyasa","sanjaya","direct-hearing","secret-teaching","krishna-arjuna-dialogue"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":76,"order":699,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"A sacred conversation keeps giving joy each time it is remembered.","snippet":"O King, remembering again and again this wondrous, holy dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna, I rejoice again and again.","tags":["sanjaya","dhritarashtra","krishna-arjuna-dialogue","smarana","gita-climax"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":77,"order":700,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Remembering Krishna\'s vast form still overwhelms the mind with wonder.","snippet":"Remembering that astonishing form of Krishna again and again, I feel great wonder, O King, and I rejoice again and again.","tags":["vishwarupa","sanjaya","awe","krishna","recollection"]},{"chapter":18,"verse":78,"order":701,"speaker":"Sanjaya","essence":"Right action carries its own victory.","snippet":"Where Krishna, the master of yoga, is present, and where Arjuna, the bow-bearer, is present, there are prosperity, victory, glory, and fi…","tags":["krishna-arjuna","sanjaya","kurukshetra","victory","righteous-order"]}]');

